                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ Reddit will switch to a 'logged-in only experience' ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <p>Reddit will become a "logged-in only experience," and the company plans to move fast, beginning testing soon in regions outside the US before flipping the switch globally.</p><p>The popular community website—home to a great many official and unofficial gaming message boards—lost one million search engine referrals per week on average in October, CEO Steve Huffman said on <a href="https://investor.redditinc.com/news-events/news-releases/news-details/2026/Reddit-Reports-Third-Quarter-2026-Results/default.aspx" target="_blank">an investor call today</a>. </p><p>The culprit, of course, was AI. A Google search that once might have led someone to a 14-year-old Reddit thread containing the answer to a rare household cleaning problem is now likely to present that answer in an AI summary, no click required.</p><p>"Google has really shifted in their relationship with the rest of the internet," Huffman said during a Q&amp;A.</p><p>The CEO emphasized, however, that most of Reddit's revenue (over 80%) comes from logged-in and app users, and said that the company will focus on establishing the site as "a direct daily habit" that doesn't rely on search traffic.</p><p>Efforts cited in that direction include algorithmic feeds, improved app design and performance, AI-powered moderation tools, and "new experiences like games and visual podcasts," the latter referring to, I believe, a feature that <a href="https://www.engadget.com/2238585/reddit-is-experimenting-with-video-and-audio-versions-of-posts/" target="_blank">uses generative AI to turn posts into videos</a>.</p><p>The switch to a logged-in only experience will also help "protect access to Reddit's extremely valuable corpus of data," Huffman said. </p><p>Reddit currently has AI training arrangements with OpenAI and Google. In the Q&amp;A portion of the call, Huffman said that Reddit has nothing to announce about those deals, but that it is in "active discussions" and that its leadership will "do what makes sense and is in the best interest for Reddit strategically and economically."</p><p>Although it reported 53% year-over-year revenue growth in its 2026 third-quarter results, as well as 16% growth in weekly active users, Reddit's share price dropped today due to a lower-than-expected forecast for the next quarter.</p> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/software/ai/reddit-will-switch-to-a-logged-in-only-experience/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ The exact details of the change are still being determined (and yep, this is about AI). ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">FFsgnDeG3YvaaTZPa87Pia</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/BCeGDVRed5pPqnVkmiJShC-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:58:10 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                <updated>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:04:17 +0000</updated>
                                                                                                                                            <category><![CDATA[AI]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Software]]></category>
                                                                                                <author><![CDATA[ tyler@pcgamer.com (Tyler Wilde) ]]></author>                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Tyler Wilde ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rGvfSUkSBEPzBAVS3jRh9E-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ &lt;p&gt;Tyler grew up in Silicon Valley during the &#039;80s and &#039;90s, playing games like Zork and Arkanoid on early PCs. He was later captivated by Myst, SimCity, Civilization, Command &amp; Conquer, all the shooters they call &quot;boomer shooters&quot; now, and PS1 classic Bushido Blade (that&#039;s right: he had Bleem!). Tyler joined PC Gamer in 2011, and today he&#039;s focused on the site&#039;s news coverage. His hobbies include amateur boxing and adding to his 1,200-plus hours in Rocket League.&lt;/p&gt; ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/BCeGDVRed5pPqnVkmiJShC-1920-80.jpg">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[SOPA Images (Getty Images)]]></media:credit>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:description><![CDATA[Reddit logo]]></media:description>                                                            <media:text><![CDATA[Reddit logo]]></media:text>
                                <media:title type="plain"><![CDATA[Reddit logo]]></media:title>
                                                    </media:content>
                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/BCeGDVRed5pPqnVkmiJShC-1920-80.jpg" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <p>Reddit will become a "logged-in only experience," and the company plans to move fast, beginning testing soon in regions outside the US before flipping the switch globally.</p><p>The popular community website—home to a great many official and unofficial gaming message boards—lost one million search engine referrals per week on average in October, CEO Steve Huffman said on <a href="https://investor.redditinc.com/news-events/news-releases/news-details/2026/Reddit-Reports-Third-Quarter-2026-Results/default.aspx" target="_blank">an investor call today</a>. </p><p>The culprit, of course, was AI. A Google search that once might have led someone to a 14-year-old Reddit thread containing the answer to a rare household cleaning problem is now likely to present that answer in an AI summary, no click required.</p><p>"Google has really shifted in their relationship with the rest of the internet," Huffman said during a Q&amp;A.</p><p>The CEO emphasized, however, that most of Reddit's revenue (over 80%) comes from logged-in and app users, and said that the company will focus on establishing the site as "a direct daily habit" that doesn't rely on search traffic.</p><p>Efforts cited in that direction include algorithmic feeds, improved app design and performance, AI-powered moderation tools, and "new experiences like games and visual podcasts," the latter referring to, I believe, a feature that <a href="https://www.engadget.com/2238585/reddit-is-experimenting-with-video-and-audio-versions-of-posts/" target="_blank">uses generative AI to turn posts into videos</a>.</p><p>The switch to a logged-in only experience will also help "protect access to Reddit's extremely valuable corpus of data," Huffman said. </p><p>Reddit currently has AI training arrangements with OpenAI and Google. In the Q&amp;A portion of the call, Huffman said that Reddit has nothing to announce about those deals, but that it is in "active discussions" and that its leadership will "do what makes sense and is in the best interest for Reddit strategically and economically."</p><p>Although it reported 53% year-over-year revenue growth in its 2026 third-quarter results, as well as 16% growth in weekly active users, Reddit's share price dropped today due to a lower-than-expected forecast for the next quarter.</p>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ How to start the Charting the Unknown DLC in Crimson Desert ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <p><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/crimson-desert/" target="_blank">Crimson Desert</a>'s Charting the Unknown has arrived, but rather than a focused story expansion, it's more about adding other elements to the existing world. </p><p>This includes endgame challenges, new housing options, a romance system, plus a sailing ship and ocean questline about exploring Pywel's treacherous coast and islands. Each feature has different unlock requirements, so here are the exact details for each.</p><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-shipbuilding-and-exploring-the-ocean"><span>Shipbuilding and exploring the ocean</span></h2><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1920px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="7Cwz8Dd7sccFD6RWMsBv5g" name="crimson-desert-dlc-unlock-5" alt="Crimson Desert DLC - Shark" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/7Cwz8Dd7sccFD6RWMsBv5g-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="1920" height="1080" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/7Cwz8Dd7sccFD6RWMsBv5g-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: Pearl Abyss)</span></figcaption></figure><ul><li>You can unlock the ability to buy or build your first ship after "Expanding the Camp" in "Gathered Will" during the "Grounds of the Sunrise" Greymane faction quest.</li><li>The quest to build your first ship will unlock, and progressing this questline will lead to the new ocean story.</li><li>You can upgrade to a medium or large ship for 1.2 million or 6 million camp funds respectively, or build either, which will cost less funds, but more materials.</li></ul><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-garden-of-trials-and-new-story-quests"><span>Garden of Trials and new story quests</span></h2><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1920px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="kmBFMrDPVVM2fesdYxUhCg" name="crimson-desert-dlc-unlock-4" alt="Crimson Desert DLC - Crab robot" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/kmBFMrDPVVM2fesdYxUhCg-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="1920" height="1080" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/kmBFMrDPVVM2fesdYxUhCg-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: Pearl Abyss)</span></figcaption></figure><p>You need to complete the main story to unlock the new Garden of Trials combat challenges. Once finished:</p><ol start="1"><li>Visit the Axiom Archive in the abyss, where you first met Alustin near the start of the game.</li><li>Turn right before the building's staircase and door to find a corridor into the new annex.</li></ol><p>There are also new story quests for Kliff, Oongka, and Damiane, which start after the main story is complete in Pailune and Demeniss, respectively, including new combat encounters in the world.</p><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-romances"><span>Romances</span></h2><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1920px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="ga9zmJZ5JjZmKQsTku547g" name="crimson-desert-dlc-unlock-3" alt="Crimson Desert DLC - Romance" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/ga9zmJZ5JjZmKQsTku547g-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="1920" height="1080" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/ga9zmJZ5JjZmKQsTku547g-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: Pearl Abyss)</span></figcaption></figure><p>Kliff, Oongka, and Damiane can each now romance specific NPCs:</p><ul><li>You can check via an NPC's interaction menu to see whether romance is possible.</li><li>After you reach 100 trust, select the "seduce" option, then once likeability is full, you can "propose".</li><li>The four witches have new faction quests that let you build trust and likeability with them as romance options.</li><li>Characters you marry can follow you or reside at your house, and you can also divorce any NPC after marrying.</li></ul><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-new-housing-and-management"><span>New housing and management</span></h2><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1920px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="Zii2fjKwxTw9HwPqG7fBCg" name="crimson-desert-dlc-unlock-1" alt="Crimson Desert DLC - House" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/Zii2fjKwxTw9HwPqG7fBCg-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="1920" height="1080" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/Zii2fjKwxTw9HwPqG7fBCg-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: Pearl Abyss)</span></figcaption></figure><p>There is a new upgraded housing mode in the expansion, plus facilities you can now manage:</p><ul><li>Unlock the Greymane Camp on Howling Hill and complete Luke's request in "Grounds of the Sunrise" to unlock new housing options.</li><li>Acquiring the Howling Hill camp will also unlock a number of "facility" icons around the map, which show what strongholds can be rented and used as new management facilities.</li><li>You'll need to liberate the region and complete its faction-related quest before you can access a facility.</li></ul><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="2e9a6354-d2fa-11f1-8a5e-51cd0df1dd69" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="2026 games" data-dimension48="2026 games" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:661px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:98.94%;"><img id="6offQUY4CXebir2TC27dMd" name="kingdom come 2 square" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/6offQUY4CXebir2TC27dMd-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="661" height="654" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/new-pc-games-2026/" target="_blank" data-dimension112="2e9a6354-d2fa-11f1-8a5e-51cd0df1dd69" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="2026 games" data-dimension48="2026 games" data-dimension25=""><strong>2026 games</strong></a>: All the upcoming games<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/the-best-pc-games/" target="_blank"><strong>Best PC games</strong></a>: Our all-time favorites<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/the-50-best-free-pc-games/" target="_blank"><strong>Free PC games</strong></a>: Freebie fest<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/best-fps-games/" target="_blank"><strong>Best FPS games</strong></a>: Finest gunplay<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/best-rpgs-of-all-time/" target="_blank"><strong>Best RPGs</strong></a>: Grand adventures<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/the-best-co-op-games/" target="_blank"><strong>Best co-op games</strong></a>: Better together</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/rpg/crimson-desert-how-to-start-charting-the-unknown-dlc/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ Unlock requirements for all of the expansion's new content. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">WYVRVR43bS8UTFzNmuisJA</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/75rcSjrDiHsTdek7NxqPzf-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
