                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ Donald Glover is heading up a PUBG live action series for Netflix ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <p>PUBG, the battle royale that lets you <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/pubg-frying-pan/" target="_blank">wear a frying pan on your ass</a> to keep it from getting shot off, is being made into a live action series for Netflix.</p><p>Narrative isn't really PUBG's strong point, but this one might be interesting for one big reason: Donald Glover is set to write, direct, and executive produce the series, and will also star in it. Stephen Glover, Donald's brother and frequent collaborator, is also attached to the project as writer and executive producer.</p><p>Glover has won numerous awards over the years for writing, acting, and music (under his stage name Childish Gambino), to the point that "list of awards and nominations received by Donald Glover" has its own remarkably lengthy <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_awards_and_nominations_received_by_Donald_Glover" target="_blank">Wikipedia page</a>. Highlights include two Primetime Emmy awards, two Golden Globes, five Grammy Awards, two Peabody Awards, and five Writers Guild of America Awards.</p><p>The upside of PUBG not having a strong pre-existing story like, say, <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/halo-tv-series-showtime/" target="_blank">Halo</a> or <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/fallout-tv-series/" target="_blank">Fallout</a> is that it affords creators the opportunity to do their own thing, and as I said, that could be very interesting indeed with Glover at the helm. His 2018 music video for <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VYOjWnS4cMY" target="_blank">This Is America</a>, built around themes of racism and gun violence in the US, was critically acclaimed and won multiple awards, but also attracted considerable controversy over its violent content. More recently, his Mr. &amp; Mrs. Smith series on Amazon Prime, which premiered in 2024, drew 16 Primetime Emmy nominations for its first season, including "Outstanding Lead Actor in a Drama Series" for Glover himself.</p><p>No other details about the upcoming PUBG show on Netflix were announced, but even so, I'm definitely curious about this one and looking forward to learning more.</p><div style="min-height: 250px;">                                <div class="kwizly-quiz kwizly-ON92mW"></div>                            </div>                            <script src="https://kwizly.com/embed/ON92mW.js" async=""></script><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="c9b025e0-d3cc-11f1-b0f6-f51d58061990" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="2026 games" data-dimension48="2026 games" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:661px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:98.94%;"><img id="6offQUY4CXebir2TC27dMd" name="kingdom come 2 square" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/6offQUY4CXebir2TC27dMd-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="661" height="654" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/new-pc-games-2026/" target="_blank" data-dimension112="c9b025e0-d3cc-11f1-b0f6-f51d58061990" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="2026 games" data-dimension48="2026 games" data-dimension25=""><strong>2026 games</strong></a>: All the upcoming games<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/the-best-pc-games/" target="_blank"><strong>Best PC games</strong></a>: Our all-time favorites<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/the-50-best-free-pc-games/" target="_blank"><strong>Free PC games</strong></a>: Freebie fest<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/best-fps-games/" target="_blank"><strong>Best FPS games</strong></a>: Finest gunplay<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/best-rpgs-of-all-time/" target="_blank"><strong>Best RPGs</strong></a>: Grand adventures<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/the-best-co-op-games/" target="_blank"><strong>Best co-op games</strong></a>: Better together</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/movies-tv/donald-glover-is-heading-up-a-pubg-live-action-series-for-netflix/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ The award-winning writer, actor, and musician is set to write, direct, produce, and star in the show. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">mAVV7ZijAhQbamyx5BGmWF</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/dopiaLycxZXskTnzmsspbc-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:13:32 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                <category><![CDATA[Movies & TV]]></category>
                                                                                                <author><![CDATA[ andy.chalk@pcgamer.com (Andy Chalk) ]]></author>                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Andy Chalk ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/hkTeZoDeGrvhQZtrNGPkbB-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ null ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/dopiaLycxZXskTnzmsspbc-1920-80.jpg">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[Getty Images - Photo by Mila Gruber/WireImage]]></media:credit>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:description><![CDATA[TOKYO, JAPAN - MARCH 26: Donald Glover attends the &quot;Super Mario Galaxy&quot; Tokyo Photocall on March 26, 2026 in Tokyo, Japan. (Photo by Mila Gruber/WireImage)]]></media:description>                                                            <media:text><![CDATA[TOKYO, JAPAN - MARCH 26: Donald Glover attends the &quot;Super Mario Galaxy&quot; Tokyo Photocall on March 26, 2026 in Tokyo, Japan. (Photo by Mila Gruber/WireImage)]]></media:text>
                                <media:title type="plain"><![CDATA[TOKYO, JAPAN - MARCH 26: Donald Glover attends the &quot;Super Mario Galaxy&quot; Tokyo Photocall on March 26, 2026 in Tokyo, Japan. (Photo by Mila Gruber/WireImage)]]></media:title>
                                                    </media:content>
                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/dopiaLycxZXskTnzmsspbc-1920-80.jpg" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <p>PUBG, the battle royale that lets you <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/pubg-frying-pan/" target="_blank">wear a frying pan on your ass</a> to keep it from getting shot off, is being made into a live action series for Netflix.</p><p>Narrative isn't really PUBG's strong point, but this one might be interesting for one big reason: Donald Glover is set to write, direct, and executive produce the series, and will also star in it. Stephen Glover, Donald's brother and frequent collaborator, is also attached to the project as writer and executive producer.</p><p>Glover has won numerous awards over the years for writing, acting, and music (under his stage name Childish Gambino), to the point that "list of awards and nominations received by Donald Glover" has its own remarkably lengthy <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_awards_and_nominations_received_by_Donald_Glover" target="_blank">Wikipedia page</a>. Highlights include two Primetime Emmy awards, two Golden Globes, five Grammy Awards, two Peabody Awards, and five Writers Guild of America Awards.</p><p>The upside of PUBG not having a strong pre-existing story like, say, <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/halo-tv-series-showtime/" target="_blank">Halo</a> or <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/fallout-tv-series/" target="_blank">Fallout</a> is that it affords creators the opportunity to do their own thing, and as I said, that could be very interesting indeed with Glover at the helm. His 2018 music video for <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VYOjWnS4cMY" target="_blank">This Is America</a>, built around themes of racism and gun violence in the US, was critically acclaimed and won multiple awards, but also attracted considerable controversy over its violent content. More recently, his Mr. &amp; Mrs. Smith series on Amazon Prime, which premiered in 2024, drew 16 Primetime Emmy nominations for its first season, including "Outstanding Lead Actor in a Drama Series" for Glover himself.</p><p>No other details about the upcoming PUBG show on Netflix were announced, but even so, I'm definitely curious about this one and looking forward to learning more.</p><div style="min-height: 250px;">                                <div class="kwizly-quiz kwizly-ON92mW"></div>                            </div>                            <script src="https://kwizly.com/embed/ON92mW.js" async=""></script><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="c9b025e0-d3cc-11f1-b0f6-f51d58061990" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="2026 games" data-dimension48="2026 games" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:661px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:98.94%;"><img id="6offQUY4CXebir2TC27dMd" name="kingdom come 2 square" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/6offQUY4CXebir2TC27dMd-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="661" height="654" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/new-pc-games-2026/" target="_blank" data-dimension112="c9b025e0-d3cc-11f1-b0f6-f51d58061990" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="2026 games" data-dimension48="2026 games" data-dimension25=""><strong>2026 games</strong></a>: All the upcoming games<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/the-best-pc-games/" target="_blank"><strong>Best PC games</strong></a>: Our all-time favorites<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/the-50-best-free-pc-games/" target="_blank"><strong>Free PC games</strong></a>: Freebie fest<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/best-fps-games/" target="_blank"><strong>Best FPS games</strong></a>: Finest gunplay<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/best-rpgs-of-all-time/" target="_blank"><strong>Best RPGs</strong></a>: Grand adventures<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/the-best-co-op-games/" target="_blank"><strong>Best co-op games</strong></a>: Better together</p></div>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ Destiny 2 unvaulting update: It sure sounds like the original Destiny is finally coming to PC ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <p>Bungie shocked the world (or at least, it shocked the world's Destiny fans) when it <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/bungie-un-cancels-destiny-vaulted-content-is-coming-back-as-new-leadership-promises-destiny-is-foundational-to-our-future/" target="_blank">un-canceled Destiny 2</a> in September, saying the game "is foundational to Bungie’s future" and promising to restore vaulted content and "return Destiny to its original promise." In a <a href="https://www.bungie.net/7/en/News/Article/bungiecommunityupdate_10_27" target="_blank">community update</a> shared today, the studio revealed more about that process, and one standout point is that it sure sounds like the original Destiny is finally coming to PC. </p><p>The update begins with a broad overview of what led up to the unvaulting announcement and what's happened since, a broad roadmap that breaks down into three sections—First Pass, Stretch Goals, and stuff that's probably not going to happen "for technical and/or strategic reasons"—and a progress bar:</p><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:602px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:30.73%;"><img id="oxMkLMNfdVtecuZVEkdUT5" name="Imported image 1 - 1793295731075" alt="Destiny 2 unvaulting timeline as of October 2026" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/oxMkLMNfdVtecuZVEkdUT5-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="602" height="185" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/oxMkLMNfdVtecuZVEkdUT5-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: Bungie)</span></figcaption></figure><p>It's worth noting up front that while things have been happening fairly quickly so far, the actual <em>Great Unvaultening </em>is still a long way off. The pre-production process is now underway and expected to run until January or February of 2027, and "from that point we <em>expect</em> full production will be about 12 months to fully complete the porting process," Bungie head of product Josh Deane said. That puts it in early 2028—assuming things go according to plan.</p><p>Deane then touched on what comes after that, referencing his comment in September that Bungie is "not done with Destiny." With caveats that "some things are subject to change in success or failure," he said that Bungie is "marching forward with a phased plan for Destiny’s future that celebrates our legacy and propels us into a new, far green country." To that end, he cited three "anchors" for players to watch for:</p><p><strong>Destiny 2 “Celebration’’ [Expect a new February Progress bar] </strong></p><ul><li>We believe we need to have a celebration in Destiny 2, beyond Monument of Triumph, for the community that provides <strong>new </strong>updates for you all to enjoy. More details to come!</li></ul><p><strong>Destiny ‘Legacy’ [Expect a new February Progress bar] </strong></p><ul><li>Our epic journey started over a decade ago, and the <strong>whole </strong>experience needs to be served to you all where you play today. Expect more information when we come back to you all early next year.</li></ul><p><strong>Redacted [TBD]</strong></p><ul><li>Launch Ventrilo Message: ‘We’re back’</li></ul><p>The second point is the one that caught our interest. Destiny 2 was (and, some PC Gamer folks would argue, still is) huge on PC, but the original game never came our way: More than a decade after it launched, it remains exclusive to consoles. </p><p>Proclaiming that "the whole experience needs to be served to you all where you play today" pretty strongly suggests to me that's going to change, and that's a big deal: Destiny 2's <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/fps/destiny-2-the-final-shape-review/" target="_blank">Final Shape expansion</a> brought an end to the 10-year Light and Darkness saga in 2024, but a lot of us never got to experience how it actually started, and I'd bet that having the opportunity to do so would bring a lot of lapsed players (myself included) back to see what's cooking.</p><p>Deane concluded by saying that this is a major undertaking and not one that will be finished quickly. "It’s important to know that this is a true reset moment for Bungie, Marathon, and Destiny. We also know time isn’t our friend; we’re playing from behind with the cards we have and I’m sure we’ll have to take more punches and make some hard decisions along the way," he said.</p><p>"Knowing we are early in incubating our future and actively working on projects to bridge us to that new home, don’t expect us to make a Destiny announcement at the TGA’s this year, or to randomly drop a logo that sets the world on fire right away.</p><p>"We get there when we get there."</p><div style="min-height: 250px;">                                <div class="kwizly-quiz kwizly-ON92mW"></div>                            </div>                            <script src="https://kwizly.com/embed/ON92mW.js" async=""></script><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="e3dbfb66-d3c1-11f1-b7b8-0393b3ab37ad" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="2026 games" data-dimension48="2026 games" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:661px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:98.94%;"><img id="6offQUY4CXebir2TC27dMd" name="kingdom come 2 square" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/6offQUY4CXebir2TC27dMd-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="661" height="654" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/new-pc-games-2026/" target="_blank" data-dimension112="e3dbfb66-d3c1-11f1-b7b8-0393b3ab37ad" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="2026 games" data-dimension48="2026 games" data-dimension25=""><strong>2026 games</strong></a>: All the upcoming games<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/the-best-pc-games/" target="_blank"><strong>Best PC games</strong></a>: Our all-time favorites<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/the-50-best-free-pc-games/" target="_blank"><strong>Free PC games</strong></a>: Freebie fest<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/best-fps-games/" target="_blank"><strong>Best FPS games</strong></a>: Finest gunplay<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/best-rpgs-of-all-time/" target="_blank"><strong>Best RPGs</strong></a>: Grand adventures<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/the-best-co-op-games/" target="_blank"><strong>Best co-op games</strong></a>: Better together</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/fps/destiny-2-unvaulting-update-it-sure-sounds-like-the-original-destiny-is-finally-coming-to-pc/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ The actual restoration of vaulting Destiny 2 content is still a long way off, but Bungie has big plans for the future. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">k6MrXuaXLonueYaKUSESSF</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/hNFdy9QWLnANQi7KxgQvg6-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:57:52 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                <updated>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 21:54:42 +0000</updated>
                                                                                                                                            <category><![CDATA[FPS]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Games]]></category>
                                                                                                <author><![CDATA[ andy.chalk@pcgamer.com (Andy Chalk) ]]></author>                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Andy Chalk ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/hkTeZoDeGrvhQZtrNGPkbB-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
