                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ It's Amnesia vs Amnesia in the 'scariest game' semifinals—vote now! ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <div  class="fancy-box"><div class="fancy_box-title">Presented by</div><div class="fancy_box_body"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' ><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="N5WXFQSCttV6Am7CopwTzd" name="Copy of 1_HeroLogo copy" caption="" alt="No More Room in Hell 2 logo" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/N5WXFQSCttV6Am7CopwTzd-1920-80.png" mos="" link="" align="" fullscreen="" width="" height="" attribution="" endorsement="" class="pinterest-pin-exclude" /></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=""><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: Torn Banner)</span></figcaption></figure><p class="fancy-box__body-text">This article is brought to you by <a data-analytics-id="inline-link" href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/292000?utm_source=future&amp;utm_medium=display&amp;utm_campaign=ppms_nmrih2_october_us&amp;utm_term=pcsteam_horror&amp;utm_creative=logo " target="_blank">No More Room in Hell 2</a>.</p></div></div><p>Last week, I asked PC Gamer readers to nominate the scariest PC games they could think of. I collected the top 16 submissions from that comment section (with some editorial discretion) and randomly seeded the bracket below.</p><p>After two rounds of voting, the field has been narrowed to just four games. This vote will determine which two games face off in the final battle on Friday, which will leave us with just one scariest game on PC, to be announced on Halloween. </p><p>Scroll on to see where the bracket stands and cast your votes in the semifinal round. Voting for this round will close on Friday at 9 am PT, and the final round will start shortly after.</p><h3 class="article-body__section" id="section-the-bracket"><span> The bracket</span></h3><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:2560px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="FQpKuEQPbshwbXbLytgbHh" name="scariest game bracket round 3" alt="The Scariest Game on PC: Round 3 bracket" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/FQpKuEQPbshwbXbLytgbHh-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="2560" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/FQpKuEQPbshwbXbLytgbHh-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: Future)</span></figcaption></figure><p>Both Amnesias made it far enough to wind up fighting each other. The deciding factor may end up being which of them has been played the most. If you want to do some research, Amnesia: The Bunker is $5 on <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/1944430/Amnesia_The_Bunker/" target="_blank">Steam</a> and <a href="https://www.gog.com/en/game/amnesia_the_bunker" target="_blank">GOG</a> right now, and The Dark Descent is <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/57300/Amnesia_The_Dark_Descent/" target="_blank">just $4</a>.</p><p>Meanwhile, Silent Hill 2 just barely beat out Dead Space for the privilege of battling tournament heavyweight Alien: Isolation. When I say 'barely,' I mean it: I had to check the vote count in the backend of our polling software to learn that Dead Space received 602 votes, and Silent Hill 2 received 614 votes.</p><h3 class="article-body__section" id="section-amnesia-the-bunker-vs-amnesia-the-dark-descent"><span>Amnesia: The Bunker vs Amnesia: The Dark Descent</span></h3><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1920px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="Wf4sUZFofJDmCH8B3WjfVf" name="the bunker vs dark descent" alt="Amnesia: The Bunker vs Amnesia: The Dark Descent" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/Wf4sUZFofJDmCH8B3WjfVf-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1920" height="1080" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline" /></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: Frictional Games)</span></figcaption></figure><div style="min-height: 250px;">                                <div class="kwizly-quiz kwizly-W3RQge"></div>                            </div>                            <script src="https://kwizly.com/embed/W3RQge.js" async=""></script><h3 class="article-body__section" id="section-silent-hill-2-vs-alien-isolation"><span>Silent Hill 2 vs Alien Isolation</span></h3><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1920px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="Lg6TZZrVrPxZPoDfi35gMf" name="silent hill 2 vs alien isolation" alt="Silent Hill 2 vs Alien: Isolation" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/Lg6TZZrVrPxZPoDfi35gMf-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1920" height="1080" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline" /></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: Konami/Creative Assembly)</span></figcaption></figure><p>Silent Hill 2 can refer to the PC version of the original, Silent Hill 2: Restless Dreams (2002), or the recent remake, Silent Hill 2 (2022). We'll say that Silent Hill 2 is a vote for either or both versions; you can specify in the comments if you like.</p><div style="min-height: 250px;">                                <div class="kwizly-quiz kwizly-WVG2PO"></div>                            </div>                            <script src="https://kwizly.com/embed/WVG2PO.js" async=""></script> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/horror/its-amnesia-vs-amnesia-in-the-scariest-game-semifinals-vote-now/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ In round three of our 'scariest game on PC' tournament, two Amnesias face off, and Silent Hill 2 takes on Alien: Isolation. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">RVPN57SfVPBfjxAhi6tyVN</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/RmkKQEKvDpQ8UywA2UKRMZ-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:29:52 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                <updated>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:32:01 +0000</updated>
                                                                                                                                            <category><![CDATA[Horror]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Games]]></category>
                                                                                                <author><![CDATA[ tyler@pcgamer.com (Tyler Wilde) ]]></author>                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Tyler Wilde ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rGvfSUkSBEPzBAVS3jRh9E-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ &lt;p&gt;Tyler grew up in Silicon Valley during the &#039;80s and &#039;90s, playing games like Zork and Arkanoid on early PCs. He was later captivated by Myst, SimCity, Civilization, Command &amp; Conquer, all the shooters they call &quot;boomer shooters&quot; now, and PS1 classic Bushido Blade (that&#039;s right: he had Bleem!). Tyler joined PC Gamer in 2011, and today he&#039;s focused on the site&#039;s news coverage. His hobbies include amateur boxing and adding to his 1,200-plus hours in Rocket League.&lt;/p&gt; ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/RmkKQEKvDpQ8UywA2UKRMZ-1920-80.jpg">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[Frictional Games]]></media:credit>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:description><![CDATA[Amnesia promo image aiming revolver at The Beast]]></media:description>                                                            <media:text><![CDATA[Amnesia promo image aiming revolver at The Beast]]></media:text>
                                <media:title type="plain"><![CDATA[Amnesia promo image aiming revolver at The Beast]]></media:title>
                                                    </media:content>
                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/RmkKQEKvDpQ8UywA2UKRMZ-1920-80.jpg" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <div  class="fancy-box"><div class="fancy_box-title">Presented by</div><div class="fancy_box_body"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' ><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="N5WXFQSCttV6Am7CopwTzd" name="Copy of 1_HeroLogo copy" caption="" alt="No More Room in Hell 2 logo" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/N5WXFQSCttV6Am7CopwTzd-1920-80.png" mos="" link="" align="" fullscreen="" width="" height="" attribution="" endorsement="" class="pinterest-pin-exclude" /></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=""><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: Torn Banner)</span></figcaption></figure><p class="fancy-box__body-text">This article is brought to you by <a data-analytics-id="inline-link" href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/292000?utm_source=future&amp;utm_medium=display&amp;utm_campaign=ppms_nmrih2_october_us&amp;utm_term=pcsteam_horror&amp;utm_creative=logo " target="_blank">No More Room in Hell 2</a>.</p></div></div><p>Last week, I asked PC Gamer readers to nominate the scariest PC games they could think of. I collected the top 16 submissions from that comment section (with some editorial discretion) and randomly seeded the bracket below.</p><p>After two rounds of voting, the field has been narrowed to just four games. This vote will determine which two games face off in the final battle on Friday, which will leave us with just one scariest game on PC, to be announced on Halloween. </p><p>Scroll on to see where the bracket stands and cast your votes in the semifinal round. Voting for this round will close on Friday at 9 am PT, and the final round will start shortly after.</p><h3 class="article-body__section" id="section-the-bracket"><span> The bracket</span></h3><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:2560px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="FQpKuEQPbshwbXbLytgbHh" name="scariest game bracket round 3" alt="The Scariest Game on PC: Round 3 bracket" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/FQpKuEQPbshwbXbLytgbHh-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="2560" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/FQpKuEQPbshwbXbLytgbHh-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: Future)</span></figcaption></figure><p>Both Amnesias made it far enough to wind up fighting each other. The deciding factor may end up being which of them has been played the most. If you want to do some research, Amnesia: The Bunker is $5 on <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/1944430/Amnesia_The_Bunker/" target="_blank">Steam</a> and <a href="https://www.gog.com/en/game/amnesia_the_bunker" target="_blank">GOG</a> right now, and The Dark Descent is <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/57300/Amnesia_The_Dark_Descent/" target="_blank">just $4</a>.</p><p>Meanwhile, Silent Hill 2 just barely beat out Dead Space for the privilege of battling tournament heavyweight Alien: Isolation. When I say 'barely,' I mean it: I had to check the vote count in the backend of our polling software to learn that Dead Space received 602 votes, and Silent Hill 2 received 614 votes.</p><h3 class="article-body__section" id="section-amnesia-the-bunker-vs-amnesia-the-dark-descent"><span>Amnesia: The Bunker vs Amnesia: The Dark Descent</span></h3><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1920px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="Wf4sUZFofJDmCH8B3WjfVf" name="the bunker vs dark descent" alt="Amnesia: The Bunker vs Amnesia: The Dark Descent" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/Wf4sUZFofJDmCH8B3WjfVf-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1920" height="1080" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline" /></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: Frictional Games)</span></figcaption></figure><div style="min-height: 250px;">                                <div class="kwizly-quiz kwizly-W3RQge"></div>                            </div>                            <script src="https://kwizly.com/embed/W3RQge.js" async=""></script><h3 class="article-body__section" id="section-silent-hill-2-vs-alien-isolation"><span>Silent Hill 2 vs Alien Isolation</span></h3><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1920px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="Lg6TZZrVrPxZPoDfi35gMf" name="silent hill 2 vs alien isolation" alt="Silent Hill 2 vs Alien: Isolation" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/Lg6TZZrVrPxZPoDfi35gMf-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1920" height="1080" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline" /></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: Konami/Creative Assembly)</span></figcaption></figure><p>Silent Hill 2 can refer to the PC version of the original, Silent Hill 2: Restless Dreams (2002), or the recent remake, Silent Hill 2 (2022). We'll say that Silent Hill 2 is a vote for either or both versions; you can specify in the comments if you like.</p><div style="min-height: 250px;">                                <div class="kwizly-quiz kwizly-WVG2PO"></div>                            </div>                            <script src="https://kwizly.com/embed/WVG2PO.js" async=""></script>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ YouTuber buys and turns 32 GB of laptop DDR5 into desktop RAM for just $175 ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <div class="youtube-video" data-nosnippet ><div class="video-aspect-box"><iframe data-lazy-priority="low" data-lazy-src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/bpT5CdOBNDU" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></div></div><p>In this week's 'what the memory crisis is doing to people' news, a YouTuber has recently bought 32 GB of DDR5 laptop memory online and successfully converted it into memory for their desktop. Overall, it cost them just $175 ($120 for the memory and $55 for extra components). That's a bit of a bargain, as 32 GB DDR5 dual-channel memory is fetching <a href="https://www.newegg.com/p/pl?d=32+GB+DDR5" target="_blank">upwards of $500 on Newegg right now.</a> </p><p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bpT5CdOBNDU" target="_blank">Blighted Agent took to their YouTube channel</a> to share the process, where they purchased two SO-DIMM sticks of 16 GB DDR5 memory on Facebook Marketplace (presumably salvaged from a dead laptop). From here, they put a stick on a preheater, then removed the BIOS chip, the SPD chip and all eight of its memory chips. </p><p>Buying new DDR5 DIMM PCBs and heatsinks off AliExpress, they cleaned the factory unleaded solder on the laptop memory, then soldered them onto the new PCBs. It's an impressive feat that requires reballing the memory chips with a stencil, a very precise procedure. </p><div style="min-height: 250px;">                                <div class="kwizly-quiz kwizly-OKyGme"></div>                            </div>                            <script src="https://kwizly.com/embed/OKyGme.js" async=""></script><p>Blighted Agent says, "You want a thin layer of flux, not too much or not too little. If you do too little, the balls might not reflow properly. If you do too much, they might bridge and cause problems". </p><p>Effectively, those solder balls connect the memory chip circuitry to the circuitry on the board, so mistakes would require redoing the entire process. From here, everything that was taken off the original SO-DIMM sticks is then put onto the new boards, tested via the desktop BIOS, before getting a heatsink. </p><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1920px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="eLnkM5Em9ob5RsJrdsaGL" name="I Turned Laptop DDR5 in Desktop DDR5 and then Overclocked It 4-7 screenshot" alt="A still from Blighted Agent's YouTube video converting laptop ram into desktop ram" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/eLnkM5Em9ob5RsJrdsaGL-1920-80.png" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1920" height="1080" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline" /></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: Blighted Agent)</span></figcaption></figure><p>Blighted Agent reports this memory kit has a 7800 MT/s frequency at CL38 when overclocked, making it a decent bit of kit and likely to cost a pretty penny as a standard RAM kit today. It reportedly tested stable for an hour and a half. They also say it worked fine without any blue screens in normal use. </p><p>Though Blighted Agent makes it look easy, technical knowledge is needed to actually convert the memory, so it's hard to recommend doing it at home unless you are willing to buy the gear and teach yourself, but this points to a decent alternate path while the <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/hardware/memory/ram-and-storage-is-ridiculously-expensive-right-now-because-of-drumroll-ai-of-course-and-theres-little-reason-to-think-prices-will-drop-any-time-soon/" target="_blank">memory crisis</a> continues to gut pricing. </p><p>One could feasibly convert memory from laptops and give it back to users for a technical fee, and still pay less than it would cost you to get the standard desktop memory. And right now, we're all looking for ways to get memory as cheap as possible. </p><p>Here's hoping AI companies don't try to buy up all the laptop memory to do the same thing. </p> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/hardware/memory/youtuber-buys-and-turns-32-gb-of-laptop-ddr5-into-desktop-ram-for-just-usd175/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ They then overclocked it. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">MauvyX59RAVS3pseGVQ7TQ</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/gr7AgY7afjVgYaSwefg3Tj-1920-80.png" type="image/png" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:55:22 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                <category><![CDATA[Memory]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Hardware]]></category>
                                                                                                                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ James Bentley ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/PVsHAkx27zJptZHndizEAE-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ &lt;p&gt;James is a more recent PC gaming convert, often admiring graphics cards, cases, and motherboards from afar. It was not until 2019, after just finishing a degree in law and media, that they decided to throw out the last few years of education, build their PC, and start writing about gaming instead. In that time, he has covered the latest doodads, contraptions, and gismos, and loved every second of it. Hey, it’s better than writing case briefs.&lt;/p&gt; ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/png" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/gr7AgY7afjVgYaSwefg3Tj-1920-80.png">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[Blighted Agent]]></media:credit>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:description><![CDATA[A still from Blighted Agent&#039;s YouTube video converting laptop ram into desktop ram]]></media:description>                                                            <media:text><![CDATA[A still from Blighted Agent&#039;s YouTube video converting laptop ram into desktop ram]]></media:text>
                                <media:title type="plain"><![CDATA[A still from Blighted Agent&#039;s YouTube video converting laptop ram into desktop ram]]></media:title>
                                                    </media:content>
                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/gr7AgY7afjVgYaSwefg3Tj-1920-80.png" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <div class="youtube-video" data-nosnippet ><div class="video-aspect-box"><iframe data-lazy-priority="low" data-lazy-src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/bpT5CdOBNDU" allowfullscreen=""></iframe></div></div><p>In this week's 'what the memory crisis is doing to people' news, a YouTuber has recently bought 32 GB of DDR5 laptop memory online and successfully converted it into memory for their desktop. Overall, it cost them just $175 ($120 for the memory and $55 for extra components). That's a bit of a bargain, as 32 GB DDR5 dual-channel memory is fetching <a href="https://www.newegg.com/p/pl?d=32+GB+DDR5" target="_blank">upwards of $500 on Newegg right now.</a> </p><p><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bpT5CdOBNDU" target="_blank">Blighted Agent took to their YouTube channel</a> to share the process, where they purchased two SO-DIMM sticks of 16 GB DDR5 memory on Facebook Marketplace (presumably salvaged from a dead laptop). From here, they put a stick on a preheater, then removed the BIOS chip, the SPD chip and all eight of its memory chips. </p><p>Buying new DDR5 DIMM PCBs and heatsinks off AliExpress, they cleaned the factory unleaded solder on the laptop memory, then soldered them onto the new PCBs. It's an impressive feat that requires reballing the memory chips with a stencil, a very precise procedure. </p><div style="min-height: 250px;">                                <div class="kwizly-quiz kwizly-OKyGme"></div>                            </div>                            <script src="https://kwizly.com/embed/OKyGme.js" async=""></script><p>Blighted Agent says, "You want a thin layer of flux, not too much or not too little. If you do too little, the balls might not reflow properly. If you do too much, they might bridge and cause problems". </p><p>Effectively, those solder balls connect the memory chip circuitry to the circuitry on the board, so mistakes would require redoing the entire process. From here, everything that was taken off the original SO-DIMM sticks is then put onto the new boards, tested via the desktop BIOS, before getting a heatsink. </p><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1920px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="eLnkM5Em9ob5RsJrdsaGL" name="I Turned Laptop DDR5 in Desktop DDR5 and then Overclocked It 4-7 screenshot" alt="A still from Blighted Agent's YouTube video converting laptop ram into desktop ram" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/eLnkM5Em9ob5RsJrdsaGL-1920-80.png" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1920" height="1080" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline" /></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: Blighted Agent)</span></figcaption></figure><p>Blighted Agent reports this memory kit has a 7800 MT/s frequency at CL38 when overclocked, making it a decent bit of kit and likely to cost a pretty penny as a standard RAM kit today. It reportedly tested stable for an hour and a half. They also say it worked fine without any blue screens in normal use. </p><p>Though Blighted Agent makes it look easy, technical knowledge is needed to actually convert the memory, so it's hard to recommend doing it at home unless you are willing to buy the gear and teach yourself, but this points to a decent alternate path while the <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/hardware/memory/ram-and-storage-is-ridiculously-expensive-right-now-because-of-drumroll-ai-of-course-and-theres-little-reason-to-think-prices-will-drop-any-time-soon/" target="_blank">memory crisis</a> continues to gut pricing. </p><p>One could feasibly convert memory from laptops and give it back to users for a technical fee, and still pay less than it would cost you to get the standard desktop memory. And right now, we're all looking for ways to get memory as cheap as possible. </p><p>Here's hoping AI companies don't try to buy up all the laptop memory to do the same thing. </p>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ I'm calling it: GTA 6 is officially an immersive sim, based on what you can do with NPCs ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <p>I don't mean to be contrarian (which is rare for me), but I've been generally unfazed by the hype for Grand Theft Auto 6. It's not that I don't think it'll be good—I'm actually damn near certain it will—it's just that none of what Rockstar has focused on so far in its marketing speaks to me all that much.</p><p>Anyway, throw those equanimous sentiments out the window, because an anecdote from <a href="https://www.magazinesdirect.com/uk/edge-subscription/dp/39f150bb">Edge magazine's</a> new mondo-feature on GTA 6 has convinced me this game is actually an immersive sim, and now I'm bouncing off the walls in anticipation. Chatting about his experience actually playing the game, Rockstar head of development Phil Hooker told a story about the time he deployed a bit of unorthodox crowd control to prepare a store for a heist.</p><p>"Recently I was robbing a store that was full of people," said Hooker. "I wanted to get rid of them, because they'd be witnesses who would cause me trouble." What did he do? Well, in GTAs of yore, your options would have been pretty limited, but GTA 6's dovetailing systems gave our man an opportunity. "I basically started picking fights with them, provoking them and then immediately defusing it.</p><p>"I didn't actually get them into a fight—I'd just go: 'Ah, sorry, leave it'. Then they would leave the store, so that would clear them out and I could rob it more cleanly." It's one of the things Hooker says he, and Rockstar generally, focuses on in testing: "meeting new NPCs, for example, trying different ways in which to interact with them, trying to find ways to combine the features in ways we maybe haven't thought about."</p><div style="min-height: 250px;">                                <div class="kwizly-quiz kwizly-ON92mW"></div>                            </div>                            <script src="https://kwizly.com/embed/ON92mW.js" async=""></script><p>Forgive me, but is that not the most immersive sim stuff you've ever heard? A sandbox crammed with systems that can collide—or be manipulated—in ways the developers themselves never even expected, to the delight and satisfaction of a creative player? I say it is, and it's quite honestly made me more excited for Rockstar's quadrillion-dollar baby than any glossy trailer. Put it in my hands, please, and then let me use those hands to pick up a crate that turns translucent when I do it.</p><p><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/grand-theft-auto/report-claims-grand-theft-auto-6-will-launch-on-pc-sooner-than-anyone-expected/">Rumor has it</a> that GTA 6 will come to PC relatively quickly after the console launch, though Rockstar typically puts at least seven months between console and PC launches. </p><div class="product star-deal"><a data-dimension112="f3b062c2-d3ab-11f1-bfbc-65437c071372" data-action="Star Deal Block" data-label="GTA 6 guide" data-dimension48="GTA 6 guide" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:948px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="kkNtsnEsZiTdgmuFTn4pJ6" name="gta 6 raul bautista square" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/kkNtsnEsZiTdgmuFTn4pJ6-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="948" height="948" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><div><span class="product__star-deal-label">Grand Theft Auto 6</span><p><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/grand-theft-auto/gta-6-guide/" data-dimension112="f3b062c2-d3ab-11f1-bfbc-65437c071372" data-action="Star Deal Block" data-label="GTA 6 guide" data-dimension48="GTA 6 guide" data-dimension25=""><strong>GTA 6 guide</strong></a>: Everything we know<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/grand-theft-auto/gta-6-pc-release-date/"><strong>GTA 6 PC release</strong></a>: When's it going to happen?<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/grand-theft-auto/gta-6-pre-order-editions-standard-ultimate"><strong>GTA 6 editions</strong></a>: What's included at each price point<br /><strong></strong><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/gta-6-cars-list/" target="_blank"><strong>GTA 6 cars</strong></a>: The known garage lineup<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/grand-theft-auto/gta-6-weapons-list/"><strong>GTA 6 guns</strong></a>: Confirmed arsenal so far</p></div></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/grand-theft-auto/im-calling-it-gta-6-is-officially-an-immersive-sim-based-on-what-you-can-do-with-npcs/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ If I see a video of Lucia stacking crates to get over a wall I'm gonna lose it. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">jyvPfAjDsyBGBYsiRe9FaX</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/BMnB7YBg5GGG7phGyXkC5a-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:21:58 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                <updated>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:36:41 +0000</updated>
                                                                                                                                            <category><![CDATA[Grand Theft Auto]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Games]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Action]]></category>
                                                                                                <author><![CDATA[ joshua.wolens@futurenet.com (Joshua Wolens) ]]></author>                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Joshua Wolens ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/oYajqiFjn2Rwz4msxoLFyP-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ &lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt; ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/BMnB7YBg5GGG7phGyXkC5a-1920-80.jpg">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[Rockstar Games]]></media:credit>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:description><![CDATA[GTA 6 Vice City screenshot]]></media:description>                                                            <media:text><![CDATA[GTA 6 Vice City screenshot]]></media:text>
                                <media:title type="plain"><![CDATA[GTA 6 Vice City screenshot]]></media:title>
                                                    </media:content>
                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/BMnB7YBg5GGG7phGyXkC5a-1920-80.jpg" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <p>I don't mean to be contrarian (which is rare for me), but I've been generally unfazed by the hype for Grand Theft Auto 6. It's not that I don't think it'll be good—I'm actually damn near certain it will—it's just that none of what Rockstar has focused on so far in its marketing speaks to me all that much.</p><p>Anyway, throw those equanimous sentiments out the window, because an anecdote from <a href="https://www.magazinesdirect.com/uk/edge-subscription/dp/39f150bb">Edge magazine's</a> new mondo-feature on GTA 6 has convinced me this game is actually an immersive sim, and now I'm bouncing off the walls in anticipation. Chatting about his experience actually playing the game, Rockstar head of development Phil Hooker told a story about the time he deployed a bit of unorthodox crowd control to prepare a store for a heist.</p><p>"Recently I was robbing a store that was full of people," said Hooker. "I wanted to get rid of them, because they'd be witnesses who would cause me trouble." What did he do? Well, in GTAs of yore, your options would have been pretty limited, but GTA 6's dovetailing systems gave our man an opportunity. "I basically started picking fights with them, provoking them and then immediately defusing it.</p><p>"I didn't actually get them into a fight—I'd just go: 'Ah, sorry, leave it'. Then they would leave the store, so that would clear them out and I could rob it more cleanly." It's one of the things Hooker says he, and Rockstar generally, focuses on in testing: "meeting new NPCs, for example, trying different ways in which to interact with them, trying to find ways to combine the features in ways we maybe haven't thought about."</p><div style="min-height: 250px;">                                <div class="kwizly-quiz kwizly-ON92mW"></div>                            </div>                            <script src="https://kwizly.com/embed/ON92mW.js" async=""></script><p>Forgive me, but is that not the most immersive sim stuff you've ever heard? A sandbox crammed with systems that can collide—or be manipulated—in ways the developers themselves never even expected, to the delight and satisfaction of a creative player? I say it is, and it's quite honestly made me more excited for Rockstar's quadrillion-dollar baby than any glossy trailer. Put it in my hands, please, and then let me use those hands to pick up a crate that turns translucent when I do it.</p><p><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/grand-theft-auto/report-claims-grand-theft-auto-6-will-launch-on-pc-sooner-than-anyone-expected/">Rumor has it</a> that GTA 6 will come to PC relatively quickly after the console launch, though Rockstar typically puts at least seven months between console and PC launches. </p><div class="product star-deal"><a data-dimension112="f3b062c2-d3ab-11f1-bfbc-65437c071372" data-action="Star Deal Block" data-label="GTA 6 guide" data-dimension48="GTA 6 guide" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:948px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="kkNtsnEsZiTdgmuFTn4pJ6" name="gta 6 raul bautista square" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/kkNtsnEsZiTdgmuFTn4pJ6-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="948" height="948" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><div><span class="product__star-deal-label">Grand Theft Auto 6</span><p><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/grand-theft-auto/gta-6-guide/" data-dimension112="f3b062c2-d3ab-11f1-bfbc-65437c071372" data-action="Star Deal Block" data-label="GTA 6 guide" data-dimension48="GTA 6 guide" data-dimension25=""><strong>GTA 6 guide</strong></a>: Everything we know<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/grand-theft-auto/gta-6-pc-release-date/"><strong>GTA 6 PC release</strong></a>: When's it going to happen?<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/grand-theft-auto/gta-6-pre-order-editions-standard-ultimate"><strong>GTA 6 editions</strong></a>: What's included at each price point<br /><strong></strong><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/gta-6-cars-list/" target="_blank"><strong>GTA 6 cars</strong></a>: The known garage lineup<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/grand-theft-auto/gta-6-weapons-list/"><strong>GTA 6 guns</strong></a>: Confirmed arsenal so far</p></div></div>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ Where to find the Hokubo region Treasure Hunt in Forza Horizon 6 ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1943px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="3epVuAUromQGwHoY2TQqEj" name="forza-6-hokubo-treasure-hunt-1" alt="Forza Horizon 6 Hokubo Treasure Hunt location" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/3epVuAUromQGwHoY2TQqEj-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="1943" height="1093" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/3epVuAUromQGwHoY2TQqEj-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: Playground Games)</span></figcaption></figure><div  class="fancy-box"><div class="fancy_box-title">Key deets</div><div class="fancy_box_body"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' ><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="uLgJFZUifRkpE3jTbwm2zk" name="forza-6-hokubo-treasure-hunt" caption="" alt="Forza Horizon 6 Hokubo Treasure Hunt chest" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/uLgJFZUifRkpE3jTbwm2zk-1920-80.jpg" mos="" link="" align="" fullscreen="" width="" height="" attribution="" endorsement="" class="pinterest-pin-exclude" /></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=""><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: Playground Games)</span></figcaption></figure><p class="fancy-box__body-text"><strong>🚘 </strong>The treasure chest is in central Hokubo at a greenhouse in the Shikisai-no-oka.</p></div></div><p>Spring has arrived in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/forza-horizon-6/" target="_blank">Forza Horizon 6</a>'s Horizon Meets series, which means a new Treasure Hunt chest to find for some seasonal points, which will help you earn some progress towards the new cars on offer.</p><p>This week's treasure chest is in central Hokubo by a greenhouse at the Shikisai-no-oka—the distinctive field of colourful strips you can see on the map. To find it:</p><ol start="1"><li>Drive along the road going northwest through Shikisai-no-oka's fields.</li><li>When the road turns east, look for the greenhouses on your left.</li><li>The chest is between these, as shown on the map above.</li></ol><p>Head there and smash the chest to get 100,000 credits, 5,000 XP, and three Season Progress. Also make sure to complete the new photo challenge, too, if you're looking for extra points.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="99e252ec-d215-11f1-9008-45cc3d943a39" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Forza Horizon 6 car list" data-dimension48="Forza Horizon 6 car list" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:800px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="XGqaMWAZJwWt5niuFeWgNB" name="forza horizon 6 boxout" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/XGqaMWAZJwWt5niuFeWgNB-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="800" height="800" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/racing/forza-horizon-6-car-list/" target="_blank" data-dimension112="99e252ec-d215-11f1-9008-45cc3d943a39" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Forza Horizon 6 car list" data-dimension48="Forza Horizon 6 car list" data-dimension25=""><strong>Forza Horizon 6 car list</strong></a>: All the rides you can collect.<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/racing/forza-horizon-6-best-cars" target="_blank"><strong>Forza Horizon 6 best cars</strong></a>: What to buy and tune.<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/racing/forza-horizon-6-treasure-car-locations/" target="_blank"><strong>Forza Horizon 6 Treasure Cars</strong></a>: Skip the clues.<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/racing/forza-horizon-6-barn-finds/" target="_blank"><strong>Forza Horizon 6 Barn Finds</strong></a>: Track down these relics.<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/racing/forza-horizon-6-review/" target="_blank"><strong>Forza Horizon 6 review</strong></a>: What we think.</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/racing/forza-horizon-6-treasure-hunt-hokubo-region-location/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ Track this chest to some greenhouses. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
