                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ For the second time this year, Galax says it's not closing down: Palit-owned graphics card brand 'continues to operate as usual' ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <p>Galax has come out in defence of its continued existence for the second time this year, following a report that incorrectly claimed the graphics card brand was closing down its factory.</p><p>In a report by El Chapuzas Informatico, citing industry sources, Palit was claimed to be closing the Galax factory. This is said to be occurring at the same time as a major reorganisation of the Galax and KFA2 brands. </p><p>Galax, a subsidiary brand of Palit, has expressly denied this claim. In, the company says its business operations are "continuing as normal". </p><div style="min-height: 250px;">                                <div class="kwizly-quiz kwizly-OKyGme"></div>                            </div>                            <script src="https://kwizly.com/embed/OKyGme.js" async=""></script><p>"Galax continues to operate as usual," a statement under both Palit and Galax letterheads, published on the <a href="https://galax.com/en/news/official-statement-regarding-galaxs-business-operations/" target="_blank">Galax website</a>, says. "No manufacturing facilities have been shut down, and Galax products remain available through our sales channels in both domestic and international markets.</p><p>That bit about internal reorganising of the Galax and KFA2 brands has some truth to it. We know that from Palit's previous statement on a rumoured Galax closure. Yep, Galax has been rumoured for chop before, and not too long ago. <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/hardware/graphics-cards/despite-recent-reports-galax-reassures-customers-that-it-has-not-pulled-an-evga-and-exited-the-graphics-card-market/" target="_blank">It last happened in April, 2026</a>.</p><p>Back then, it was speculated that Galax was shuttering and Palit was taking over. Palit said no, Galax is still operating and we've already taken over (Palit has owned Galax since before it was officially called Galax, buying the company then named Galaxy in 2008); however, Palit did note at the time that it was integrating management of the brand, alongside KFA2 and HOF, under Palit's HQ.</p><p>So, the reports of Galax's death are greatly exaggerated, but the ones about putting it under new centralised management are closer to the mark. Importantly, the brand's cards are still on the shelves, including the brand-new <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/hardware/graphics-cards/i-have-neither-the-budget-nor-the-inclination-for-a-crystal-encrusted-rtx-5090-but-galax-is-releasing-one-anyway/" target="_blank">Galax RTX 5080 HOF Extreme encrusted with Swarovski crystals</a>.</p> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/hardware/graphics-cards/for-the-second-time-this-year-galax-says-its-not-closing-down-palit-owned-graphics-card-brand-continues-to-operate-as-usual/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ Reports of the brand's death have been greatly exaggerated. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">ZjV68X95gcbwJ3hQpxx7zU</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/NGaF45ZBzit4cYz93MhAMg-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 10:29:32 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                <category><![CDATA[Graphics Cards]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Hardware]]></category>
                                                                                                                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Jacob Ridley ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/2YNigoLXbckPdRPDe3stwA-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ &lt;p&gt;Jacob earned his first byline writing for his own tech blog, before graduating to breaking things professionally at PCGamesN, where he was one half of a popular weekly YouTube show. Joining PC Gamer in 2020, Jacob is now managing editor of the hardware team, and you&#039;ll usually find him testing the latest components or building a gaming PC. He says he&#039;s determined to build a fort as big as a house out of case boxes. Jacob enjoys heading out of the office to report from floors, benches, and, if he&#039;s lucky, plush press rooms at the biggest tech shows, such as Computex and CES.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;When he&#039;s not writing about components, you&#039;ll find Jacob trying to get away from the modern world as fast as possible by bike and pitching up camp in murky woods.&lt;/p&gt; ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/NGaF45ZBzit4cYz93MhAMg-1920-80.jpg">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[Galax]]></media:credit>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:description><![CDATA[Galax GPU on a white background.]]></media:description>                                                            <media:text><![CDATA[Galax GPU on a white background.]]></media:text>
                                <media:title type="plain"><![CDATA[Galax GPU on a white background.]]></media:title>
                                                    </media:content>
                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/NGaF45ZBzit4cYz93MhAMg-1920-80.jpg" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <p>Galax has come out in defence of its continued existence for the second time this year, following a report that incorrectly claimed the graphics card brand was closing down its factory.</p><p>In a report by El Chapuzas Informatico, citing industry sources, Palit was claimed to be closing the Galax factory. This is said to be occurring at the same time as a major reorganisation of the Galax and KFA2 brands. </p><p>Galax, a subsidiary brand of Palit, has expressly denied this claim. In, the company says its business operations are "continuing as normal". </p><div style="min-height: 250px;">                                <div class="kwizly-quiz kwizly-OKyGme"></div>                            </div>                            <script src="https://kwizly.com/embed/OKyGme.js" async=""></script><p>"Galax continues to operate as usual," a statement under both Palit and Galax letterheads, published on the <a href="https://galax.com/en/news/official-statement-regarding-galaxs-business-operations/" target="_blank">Galax website</a>, says. "No manufacturing facilities have been shut down, and Galax products remain available through our sales channels in both domestic and international markets.</p><p>That bit about internal reorganising of the Galax and KFA2 brands has some truth to it. We know that from Palit's previous statement on a rumoured Galax closure. Yep, Galax has been rumoured for chop before, and not too long ago. <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/hardware/graphics-cards/despite-recent-reports-galax-reassures-customers-that-it-has-not-pulled-an-evga-and-exited-the-graphics-card-market/" target="_blank">It last happened in April, 2026</a>.</p><p>Back then, it was speculated that Galax was shuttering and Palit was taking over. Palit said no, Galax is still operating and we've already taken over (Palit has owned Galax since before it was officially called Galax, buying the company then named Galaxy in 2008); however, Palit did note at the time that it was integrating management of the brand, alongside KFA2 and HOF, under Palit's HQ.</p><p>So, the reports of Galax's death are greatly exaggerated, but the ones about putting it under new centralised management are closer to the mark. Importantly, the brand's cards are still on the shelves, including the brand-new <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/hardware/graphics-cards/i-have-neither-the-budget-nor-the-inclination-for-a-crystal-encrusted-rtx-5090-but-galax-is-releasing-one-anyway/" target="_blank">Galax RTX 5080 HOF Extreme encrusted with Swarovski crystals</a>.</p>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ How to complete Four Fierce Axes in Phantom Blade Zero ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <p>The Four Fierce Axes quest is likely the second you'll acquire in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a>, after <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank">Flesh Lily</a>, when you find a "Four Axes" case file in the Broken Puppet Valley early on.</p><p>You'll have to "uncover the truth behind the Four Axes Rebellion" which involves continuing to the outpost and defeating the Peng Meng boss there. After that, you'll have to "gather evidence of the conspiracy against the Four Axes", which means finding seven more "Four Axes" case files in Weeping Creek Valley, besides the one you already have and one Peng Meng drops. Here's where they all are:</p><ol start="1"><li>Near the Broken Puppet Valley bell in the house on the table.</li></ol><ol start="2"><li>Also in the Broken Puppet Valley on the corpse by the shrine.</li></ol><ol start="3"><li>After the Rustblade Pavillion bell, before the Outpost Courtyard bell, on a table in the area where the game gives you a tutorial to jump assassinate a man by a campfire.</li></ol><ol start="4"><li>Near the Axemaster's Holding Cell bell on a table in the area where The Hunt has killed everyone.</li></ol><ol start="5"><li>After you acquire The Hunter's Chain Sickle and use it to get the Sha Chi Tower Base Camp Key from the top of the Sha-Chi Tower, use it to unlock the door by the Creek Valley Plains Entrance bell, and search the lower level of the tower to find it on a table in the forge area.</li></ol><ol start="6"><li>Through the Festering Secret quest. Use the Dread Axe to smash the barrier in the outpost after you defeat Peng Meng, defeat the enemies, speak to the captain, and deliver the letter to the lieutenant at the Long Pillar Overlook bell in the area you unlocked above. He'll give you the sixth case file.</li></ol><figure role="gallery"><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/ssCAML8T4pSdCczrAbiTm-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Four Fierce Axes - First case file" /><figcaption>The first case file you find in Broken Puppet Valley starts the quest<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/DXMbdVXMpDuTgAqv56J5x-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Four Fierce Axes - Peng Meng" /><figcaption>Defeat Peng Meng, The Axemaster, who also drops a case file<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/Sa2eEsC7trcFgHfuM2Lyw-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Four Fierce Axes - The key" /><figcaption>Use the Hunter's Sickles to retrieve the key on top of Sha-Chi Tower to unlock the area with the 5th and 6th files<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/iU8roAvveiGcTEMaSedxU-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Four Fierce Axes - 6th case file" /><figcaption>The 6th case file comes from the Lieutenant in the Festering Secret quest<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/77CF9exPrLbTe6gRWqrVn-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Four Fierce Axes - Final case file" /><figcaption>The 7th case file isn't accessible until you the reach the Village of Lu and the Leave None Alive quest starts<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure></figure><p>Thankfully, all of these locations are marked on your map, which makes things easier. "Hang on, that's only six out of seven, though" you may be thinking. </p><p>To get the seventh case file, you need to progress to the Village of Lu region after the Crimson Forest. You'll get the Leave None Alive quest, which directs you to head back to the outpost, and upon arriving, you'll find you're now able to get past the barrier to the location of the final case file. </p><p>Simply head into the area with the houses, up into the Lady's Cave, follow it through and outside, where you can use the Hunter's Sickles to reach the platform with the last case file.</p><h2 id="deliver-the-evidence-to-the-child-of-insight-in-pangzhen">Deliver the evidence to the Child of Insight in Pangzhen</h2><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:2560px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="C4Ba6WtsELz7ikc8Bs2nx" name="phantom-blade-zero-four-fierce-axes-8" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Four Fierce Axes - Child of Insight" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/C4Ba6WtsELz7ikc8Bs2nx-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="2560" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/C4Ba6WtsELz7ikc8Bs2nx-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: S-Game Studios)</span></figcaption></figure><p>The final step of this quest is bringing all the evidence to the Child of Insight in Pangzhen, the game's 4th region. You'll have to progress through the Village of Lu area to reach Pangzhen, then a little way into the town itself—thankfully, you'll also have a map marker for this, so it's straightforward enough. </p><p>Fight the Shadow Order guarding the marked building near the Pavillion of Knowledge Crossroads bell, then battle through three floors of masked enemies to get the key to the roof. Open the door on the top floor to find the Child of Insight standing on the roof outside and then speak to him about the Axemaster to get your reward, the Blood Oath Dagger, which Soul Tempers the Dread Axe once you unlock the ability to do so with Myst at the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-enter-orders-underground-tavern" target="_blank">Orders underground tavern</a>.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="22a15fc4-d2e8-11f1-ad3d-bd390efb384d" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="22a15fc4-d2e8-11f1-ad3d-bd390efb384d" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-four-fierce-axes-walkthrough/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ Gather evidence of the conspiracy against the Four Axes. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">J8EguWYDuGP8AQkUbnPiSW</guid>
