                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/55ZrkDzWkYPmUK5ghtQZh-1920-80.jpg" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <p>The Four Fierce Axes quest is likely the second you'll acquire in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a>, after <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank">Flesh Lily</a>, when you find a "Four Axes" case file in the Broken Puppet Valley early on.</p><p>You'll have to "uncover the truth behind the Four Axes Rebellion" which involves continuing to the outpost and defeating the Peng Meng boss there. After that, you'll have to "gather evidence of the conspiracy against the Four Axes", which means finding seven more "Four Axes" case files in Weeping Creek Valley, besides the one you already have and one Peng Meng drops. Here's where they all are:</p><ol start="1"><li>Near the Broken Puppet Valley bell in the house on the table.</li></ol><ol start="2"><li>Also in the Broken Puppet Valley on the corpse by the shrine.</li></ol><ol start="3"><li>After the Rustblade Pavillion bell, before the Outpost Courtyard bell, on a table in the area where the game gives you a tutorial to jump assassinate a man by a campfire.</li></ol><ol start="4"><li>Near the Axemaster's Holding Cell bell on a table in the area where The Hunt has killed everyone.</li></ol><ol start="5"><li>After you acquire The Hunter's Chain Sickle and use it to get the Sha Chi Tower Base Camp Key from the top of the Sha-Chi Tower, use it to unlock the door by the Creek Valley Plains Entrance bell, and search the lower level of the tower to find it on a table in the forge area.</li></ol><ol start="6"><li>Through the Festering Secret quest. Use the Dread Axe to smash the barrier in the outpost after you defeat Peng Meng, defeat the enemies, speak to the captain, and deliver the letter to the lieutenant at the Long Pillar Overlook bell in the area you unlocked above. He'll give you the sixth case file.</li></ol><figure role="gallery"><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/ssCAML8T4pSdCczrAbiTm-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Four Fierce Axes - First case file" /><figcaption>The first case file you find in Broken Puppet Valley starts the quest<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/DXMbdVXMpDuTgAqv56J5x-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Four Fierce Axes - Peng Meng" /><figcaption>Defeat Peng Meng, The Axemaster, who also drops a case file<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/Sa2eEsC7trcFgHfuM2Lyw-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Four Fierce Axes - The key" /><figcaption>Use the Hunter's Sickles to retrieve the key on top of Sha-Chi Tower to unlock the area with the 5th and 6th files<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/iU8roAvveiGcTEMaSedxU-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Four Fierce Axes - 6th case file" /><figcaption>The 6th case file comes from the Lieutenant in the Festering Secret quest<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/77CF9exPrLbTe6gRWqrVn-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Four Fierce Axes - Final case file" /><figcaption>The 7th case file isn't accessible until you the reach the Village of Lu and the Leave None Alive quest starts<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure></figure><p>Thankfully, all of these locations are marked on your map, which makes things easier. "Hang on, that's only six out of seven, though" you may be thinking. </p><p>To get the seventh case file, you need to progress to the Village of Lu region after the Crimson Forest. You'll get the Leave None Alive quest, which directs you to head back to the outpost, and upon arriving, you'll find you're now able to get past the barrier to the location of the final case file. </p><p>Simply head into the area with the houses, up into the Lady's Cave, follow it through and outside, where you can use the Hunter's Sickles to reach the platform with the last case file.</p><h2 id="deliver-the-evidence-to-the-child-of-insight-in-pangzhen">Deliver the evidence to the Child of Insight in Pangzhen</h2><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:2560px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="C4Ba6WtsELz7ikc8Bs2nx" name="phantom-blade-zero-four-fierce-axes-8" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Four Fierce Axes - Child of Insight" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/C4Ba6WtsELz7ikc8Bs2nx-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="2560" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/C4Ba6WtsELz7ikc8Bs2nx-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: S-Game Studios)</span></figcaption></figure><p>The final step of this quest is bringing all the evidence to the Child of Insight in Pangzhen, the game's 4th region. You'll have to progress through the Village of Lu area to reach Pangzhen, then a little way into the town itself—thankfully, you'll also have a map marker for this, so it's straightforward enough. </p><p>Fight the Shadow Order guarding the marked building near the Pavillion of Knowledge Crossroads bell, then battle through three floors of masked enemies to get the key to the roof. Open the door on the top floor to find the Child of Insight standing on the roof outside and then speak to him about the Axemaster to get your reward, the Blood Oath Dagger, which Soul Tempers the Dread Axe once you unlock the ability to do so with Myst at the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-enter-orders-underground-tavern" target="_blank">Orders underground tavern</a>.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="22a15fc4-d2e8-11f1-ad3d-bd390efb384d" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="22a15fc4-d2e8-11f1-ad3d-bd390efb384d" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ All Honor Among Thieves answers in Phantom Blade Zero ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <p>The Honor Among Thieves quest in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a> is relatively short—you kill an enemy in the Crimson Forest who drops a letter, which you then deliver to his brother in the Thieves Camp a little further down the trail after Jing Ye.</p><p>The brother, however, can't read, and demands you answer some questions about its contents to prove it's genuine. The answers to his questions are:</p><ol start="1"><li>Stole a landowner's belt.</li><li>Butterfly.</li><li>The letter never said. His fate is unknown.</li></ol><p>Don't worry if you get an answer wrong, he'll just end the conversation and you'll have to talk to him again. These answers are, of course, in the letter itself. Look for the Wulin Tales section of the archive and then the 8th entry, Blood Letter from the Nimble Thief.</p><p>Answer all three correctly and you'll get the Silent Wrap accessory, which reduces noise from assassinations and movement by 40%, though you can upgrade this further once you unlock polishing in the Village of Lu.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="549f8c4c-d2ea-11f1-bc38-2106467f82cd" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="549f8c4c-d2ea-11f1-bc38-2106467f82cd" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-honor-among-thieves-answers-gentle-thief-questions/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ Describe the brother's letter to The Gentle Thief. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">2A3RTCyU3GP3njmeWhFaS3</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rNgzBpsp66EgNgxdQbG75o-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                <category><![CDATA[Action]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Games]]></category>
                                                                                                                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Sean Martin ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rw7hUY3Y2mxZJtwx3ePdwF-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ null ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rNgzBpsp66EgNgxdQbG75o-1920-80.jpg">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[S-Game Studios]]></media:credit>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:description><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Honor Among Thieves]]></media:description>                                                            <media:text><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Honor Among Thieves]]></media:text>
                                <media:title type="plain"><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Honor Among Thieves]]></media:title>
                                                    </media:content>
                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rNgzBpsp66EgNgxdQbG75o-1920-80.jpg" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <p>The Honor Among Thieves quest in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a> is relatively short—you kill an enemy in the Crimson Forest who drops a letter, which you then deliver to his brother in the Thieves Camp a little further down the trail after Jing Ye.</p><p>The brother, however, can't read, and demands you answer some questions about its contents to prove it's genuine. The answers to his questions are:</p><ol start="1"><li>Stole a landowner's belt.</li><li>Butterfly.</li><li>The letter never said. His fate is unknown.</li></ol><p>Don't worry if you get an answer wrong, he'll just end the conversation and you'll have to talk to him again. These answers are, of course, in the letter itself. Look for the Wulin Tales section of the archive and then the 8th entry, Blood Letter from the Nimble Thief.</p><p>Answer all three correctly and you'll get the Silent Wrap accessory, which reduces noise from assassinations and movement by 40%, though you can upgrade this further once you unlock polishing in the Village of Lu.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="549f8c4c-d2ea-11f1-bc38-2106467f82cd" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="549f8c4c-d2ea-11f1-bc38-2106467f82cd" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ I've spent over 50 hours in Phantom Blade Zero—here are my top 20 tips to conquer the Wulin ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <div class="card card--standard card--rows-3 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/U6TV3QB2RYzmu2bHJJwc7P.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Blackstone" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">1. Explore thoroughly</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Attack power, Sha-Chi (stamina) and HP are increased by collectibles you find or get by defeating enemy encounters. Specifically: Blackstone, Sha-Chi Amber, and Memory Flowers.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/9TBtsPCsGyXL6T32UqtNLP.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Wall markings" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">2. Examine everything</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Investigating objects or notes rewards Remnant Dust (souls) in Phantom Blade Zero, but can also reveal new sidequests.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rzqiZ2YapugCsRsSmm4xVg.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Soul and Zhou" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">3. Attack constantly</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Your regular attacks (X on controller) don't consume stamina, but they will deal damage and chip down a boss's Sha-Chi, so be aggressive.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-3 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/ioY3fJPxKfNvCRbvmf4uiP.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Memory Flower" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">4. Collect Memory Flowers</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Besides granting HP and story fragments, collecting all Memory Flowers before a region boss often gives them an extra phase or sometimes a unique reward, such as a weapon. You'll be introduced to these in the Crimson Forest.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/RbYSrNk2eKvyJQMoE899vP.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Red attack" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">5. Remember red is right, blue is left</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>When an attack flashes red, hit the right bumper on controller. When it flashes blue, hit the left. Or if you're struggling to react or remember, just hit both.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/Zvx9KTYJ4Y7uhn53Chc5vP.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Black attack" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">6. Dodge smoky black attacks also</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>You'll first experience these stamina-draining attacks fighting Peng Meng, where the boss emits a smoky black aura. Dodge these instead of blocking to retain your Sha-Chi.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-3 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/6dqi9XLR4oAoSBKbCpgnnP.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Maskwalkers" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">7. Use Sha-Chi combos to deal damage</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Your Sha-Chi combos (Y on controller) cost stamina, but deal more damage—use these after you parry a red or blue attack, or when you've broken your opponent's Sha-Chi, meaning they can't block for a while.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/4nA8yjPLJU5QrJ9QCyrTmb.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Juggernaut" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">8. Experiment with weapons</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>You can refund all materials and Remnant Dust from an upgraded weapon or Phantom Edge. It's free up to Level 10. After that it costs a reforge talisman, which are easy to find.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/aSbPgEBa5FdJs9XZbCS8vC.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero best weapon - Jagged Steel" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">9. Pay attention to your skills</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Every five upgrade levels a weapon or Phantom Edge gain a new ability, either passive or active—make sure to learn what these are to use them in combat.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-3 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/r9ETMiFQuW4SQHcNzBSr7P.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Phantom Edge" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">10. Use your Phantom Edges</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Unlike Sekiro, where Shinobi tools cost a limited talisman resource, you get a fixed amount of sparks (Phantom Edge uses) every time you rest, plus you can recoup them using certain skills and accessories.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/VzSvRaVc5EohmC7kwUrknN.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Bell" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">11. Rest at bells often</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Resting at bells in Phantom Blade Zero doesn't reset enemies as in soulslikes, but it will replenish your medicine healing items and spark uses for Phantom Edges.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/Wci2cTaU5tvJswEMCdKYvP.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Soldiers" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">12. Counter for free</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>When you see an RT (on controller) appear on an enemy, it means you can use your equipped Phantom Edge without it costing a spark, so make sure to take advantage of this.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-3 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/isRDGbJSPcwWvLyZ2rBPBP.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Forge" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">13.  Use weapons of different types</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>I'd suggest a one-handed and two-handed weapon. Different weapons have different strengths, but each type uses a separate upgrade material. Some weapons, like <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-best-weapon-jagged-steel" target="_blank">Jagged Steel</a>, deal statuses which are only effective against some enemies.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/QtoAx5ghF6y92Kn5XbN8vP.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Jewel" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">14. Polish your accessories</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Accessories are very strong, especially as you unlock more slots and the ability to buff their effect when you arrive in the Village of Lu. Besides weapons, this is where your build comes from.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/55ZrkDzWkYPmUK5ghtQZh.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Four Fierce Axes - Peng Meng" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">15. You can die lots</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Unlike soulslikes, you don't lose Remnant Echoes when you die in Phantom Blade Zero and even if you die to a boss during its second phase, you'll start the fight from that same phase.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-3 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/AjYq5aFozPboLgTEmmR5vP.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Assassination" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">16. Don&#39;t forget about stealth</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>It's introduced in the early game, but it's easy to forget you can go stealth anytime. Assassinations, in particular, are very strong, as you can often follow up to assassinate a second enemy nearby.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/RyvXsvh6fYW3iFBENnyWpm.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero upgrade medicine - Apprentice Healer" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">17. Upgrade your medicine</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>This won't be available until later in the Pangzheng region, but <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-upgrade-medicine" target="_blank">levelling your medicine</a> buffs the amount of healing, stamina, or damage negation it applies, as well as providing extra uses.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/N2mf2bj7nLarUx9Xx2vSwj.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Banyan Tree" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">18. Complete Banyan Trees</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Some abilities require <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-banyans-heart-location" target="_blank">T</a><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-banyans-heart-location">he</a><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-banyans-heart-location"> Banyan's Heart</a> to upgrade, which involves completing a combat trials to earn the item. There are five of these trees in the game, but you can also buy a few hearts as well.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/qniH4fbtB46g8AUcnp2BVY.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Yu'er" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">19. Some quests are missable</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>If you have a quest with tracking markers located in your current region that you can reach or access, it's a good idea to finish it before you leave. Some quests can fail, though there are plenty where you're expected to return later also. </p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/tvsRt3GHFBWp5XERzvf8vP.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Challenge" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">20. Come back later</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>If you're struggling with an optional boss, such as the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-aberrant-three-faced-puppet-triple-threat">Aberrant Three-Faced Puppet</a> or <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-gold-masked-one-boss-guide">Gold-Masked One</a>, remember you can come back later. Phantom Blade Zero doesn't have many points of no return, so you have plenty of time to get stronger.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="bcc86532-d2e5-11f1-9b77-ad1a73c3a434" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank" data-dimension112="bcc86532-d2e5-11f1-9b77-ad1a73c3a434" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-crimson-manor-enter" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Crimson Manor</strong></a>: Open the door<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips/</link>
