                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <div class="card card--standard card--rows-3 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/U6TV3QB2RYzmu2bHJJwc7P.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Blackstone" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">1. Explore thoroughly</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Attack power, Sha-Chi (stamina) and HP are increased by collectibles you find or get by defeating enemy encounters. Specifically: Blackstone, Sha-Chi Amber, and Memory Flowers.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/9TBtsPCsGyXL6T32UqtNLP.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Wall markings" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">2. Examine everything</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Investigating objects or notes rewards Remnant Dust (souls) in Phantom Blade Zero, but can also reveal new sidequests.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rzqiZ2YapugCsRsSmm4xVg.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Soul and Zhou" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">3. Attack constantly</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Your regular attacks (X on controller) don't consume stamina, but they will deal damage and chip down a boss's Sha-Chi, so be aggressive.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-3 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/ioY3fJPxKfNvCRbvmf4uiP.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Memory Flower" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">4. Collect Memory Flowers</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Besides granting HP and story fragments, collecting all Memory Flowers before a region boss often gives them an extra phase or sometimes a unique reward, such as a weapon. You'll be introduced to these in the Crimson Forest.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/RbYSrNk2eKvyJQMoE899vP.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Red attack" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">5. Remember red is right, blue is left</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>When an attack flashes red, hit the right bumper on controller. When it flashes blue, hit the left. Or if you're struggling to react or remember, just hit both.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/Zvx9KTYJ4Y7uhn53Chc5vP.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Black attack" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">6. Dodge smoky black attacks also</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>You'll first experience these stamina-draining attacks fighting Peng Meng, where the boss emits a smoky black aura. Dodge these instead of blocking to retain your Sha-Chi.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-3 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/6dqi9XLR4oAoSBKbCpgnnP.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Maskwalkers" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">7. Use Sha-Chi combos to deal damage</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Your Sha-Chi combos (Y on controller) cost stamina, but deal more damage—use these after you parry a red or blue attack, or when you've broken your opponent's Sha-Chi, meaning they can't block for a while.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/4nA8yjPLJU5QrJ9QCyrTmb.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Juggernaut" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">8. Experiment with weapons</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>You can refund all materials and Remnant Dust from an upgraded weapon or Phantom Edge. It's free up to Level 10. After that it costs a reforge talisman, which are easy to find.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/aSbPgEBa5FdJs9XZbCS8vC.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero best weapon - Jagged Steel" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">9. Pay attention to your skills</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Every five upgrade levels a weapon or Phantom Edge gain a new ability, either passive or active—make sure to learn what these are to use them in combat.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-3 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/r9ETMiFQuW4SQHcNzBSr7P.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Phantom Edge" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">10. Use your Phantom Edges</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Unlike Sekiro, where Shinobi tools cost a limited talisman resource, you get a fixed amount of sparks (Phantom Edge uses) every time you rest, plus you can recoup them using certain skills and accessories.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/VzSvRaVc5EohmC7kwUrknN.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Bell" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">11. Rest at bells often</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Resting at bells in Phantom Blade Zero doesn't reset enemies as in soulslikes, but it will replenish your medicine healing items and spark uses for Phantom Edges.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/Wci2cTaU5tvJswEMCdKYvP.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Soldiers" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">12. Counter for free</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>When you see an RT (on controller) appear on an enemy, it means you can use your equipped Phantom Edge without it costing a spark, so make sure to take advantage of this.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-3 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/isRDGbJSPcwWvLyZ2rBPBP.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Forge" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">13.  Use weapons of different types</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>I'd suggest a one-handed and two-handed weapon. Different weapons have different strengths, but each type uses a separate upgrade material. Some weapons, like <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-best-weapon-jagged-steel" target="_blank">Jagged Steel</a>, deal statuses which are only effective against some enemies.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/QtoAx5ghF6y92Kn5XbN8vP.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Jewel" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">14. Polish your accessories</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Accessories are very strong, especially as you unlock more slots and the ability to buff their effect when you arrive in the Village of Lu. Besides weapons, this is where your build comes from.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/55ZrkDzWkYPmUK5ghtQZh.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Four Fierce Axes - Peng Meng" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">15. You can die lots</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Unlike soulslikes, you don't lose Remnant Echoes when you die in Phantom Blade Zero and even if you die to a boss during its second phase, you'll start the fight from that same phase.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-3 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/AjYq5aFozPboLgTEmmR5vP.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Assassination" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">16. Don&#39;t forget about stealth</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>It's introduced in the early game, but it's easy to forget you can go stealth anytime. Assassinations, in particular, are very strong, as you can often follow up to assassinate a second enemy nearby.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/RyvXsvh6fYW3iFBENnyWpm.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero upgrade medicine - Apprentice Healer" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">17. Upgrade your medicine</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>This won't be available until later in the Pangzheng region, but <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-upgrade-medicine" target="_blank">levelling your medicine</a> buffs the amount of healing, stamina, or damage negation it applies, as well as providing extra uses.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/N2mf2bj7nLarUx9Xx2vSwj.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Banyan Tree" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">18. Complete Banyan Trees</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>Some abilities require <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-banyans-heart-location" target="_blank">T</a><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-banyans-heart-location">he</a><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-banyans-heart-location"> Banyan's Heart</a> to upgrade, which involves completing a combat trials to earn the item. There are five of these trees in the game, but you can also buy a few hearts as well.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/qniH4fbtB46g8AUcnp2BVY.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Yu'er" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">19. Some quests are missable</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>If you have a quest with tracking markers located in your current region that you can reach or access, it's a good idea to finish it before you leave. Some quests can fail, though there are plenty where you're expected to return later also. </p></div></div></div></div><div class="card card--standard card--rows-2 card--align-inline"><div class="card-image-widthsetter"><p class="vanilla-image-block"  style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img style="width: 100%" class="card__image" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/tvsRt3GHFBWp5XERzvf8vP.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero tips - Challenge" /></p></div><div class="card__content"><h3 class="card__title">20. Come back later</h3><div class="card__description-wrapper"><div class="card__description"><p>If you're struggling with an optional boss, such as the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-aberrant-three-faced-puppet-triple-threat">Aberrant Three-Faced Puppet</a> or <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-gold-masked-one-boss-guide">Gold-Masked One</a>, remember you can come back later. Phantom Blade Zero doesn't have many points of no return, so you have plenty of time to get stronger.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="bcc86532-d2e5-11f1-9b77-ad1a73c3a434" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank" data-dimension112="bcc86532-d2e5-11f1-9b77-ad1a73c3a434" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-crimson-manor-enter" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Crimson Manor</strong></a>: Open the door<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ How to upgrade medicine in Phantom Blade Zero ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <figure role="gallery"><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/H69NmxGmr2CnLfeGcuEAkm-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero upgrade medicine menu" /><figcaption>You can upgrade your medicine using healer's memories at the Green Serpent House<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/WqqLLcbVZULFt9BehrVcpm-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero upgrade medicine - Green Serpent Brew" /><figcaption>You'll also get the Green Serpent Brew when you visit for the first time<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure></figure><p>Upgrading medicine in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a> improves the percentage of HP, damage negation, and Sha-Chi that these healing consumables replenish, which is pretty powerful, as you'd imagine.</p><p>You can upgrade your medicine when you reach the Green Serpent House in west Pangzhen (the game's 4th region after the Village of Lu). You'll arrive at this location during Pangzhen's second chapter, which sees you exploring the west side of the town, specifically, after you defeat Xie Qiudong, The Divine Healer and progress down the street, where you'll spot a big house with green banners and the Green Serpent House bell.</p><p>The Apprentice Healer here will upgrade your medicine using Apprentice Healer's Memories and Skilled Healer's Memories, some of which you likely will have already picked up during your explorations. You'll also get the Green Serpent Brew medicine, which removes status effects, when you visit for the first time.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="15039d1a-d2ec-11f1-8969-7dcbed409bf1" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="15039d1a-d2ec-11f1-8969-7dcbed409bf1" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-crimson-manor-enter" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Crimson Manor</strong></a>: Open the door<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-upgrade-medicine/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ Buff your healing items with healer's memories. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">8dt5GCyHpKQNChVjBsHCwS</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/RyvXsvh6fYW3iFBENnyWpm-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                <category><![CDATA[Action]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Games]]></category>
                                                                                                                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Sean Martin ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rw7hUY3Y2mxZJtwx3ePdwF-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ null ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/RyvXsvh6fYW3iFBENnyWpm-1920-80.jpg">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[S-Game Studios]]></media:credit>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:description><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero upgrade medicine - Apprentice Healer]]></media:description>                                                            <media:text><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero upgrade medicine - Apprentice Healer]]></media:text>
                                <media:title type="plain"><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero upgrade medicine - Apprentice Healer]]></media:title>
                                                    </media:content>
                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/RyvXsvh6fYW3iFBENnyWpm-1920-80.jpg" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <figure role="gallery"><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/H69NmxGmr2CnLfeGcuEAkm-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero upgrade medicine menu" /><figcaption>You can upgrade your medicine using healer's memories at the Green Serpent House<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/WqqLLcbVZULFt9BehrVcpm-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero upgrade medicine - Green Serpent Brew" /><figcaption>You'll also get the Green Serpent Brew when you visit for the first time<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure></figure><p>Upgrading medicine in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a> improves the percentage of HP, damage negation, and Sha-Chi that these healing consumables replenish, which is pretty powerful, as you'd imagine.</p><p>You can upgrade your medicine when you reach the Green Serpent House in west Pangzhen (the game's 4th region after the Village of Lu). You'll arrive at this location during Pangzhen's second chapter, which sees you exploring the west side of the town, specifically, after you defeat Xie Qiudong, The Divine Healer and progress down the street, where you'll spot a big house with green banners and the Green Serpent House bell.</p><p>The Apprentice Healer here will upgrade your medicine using Apprentice Healer's Memories and Skilled Healer's Memories, some of which you likely will have already picked up during your explorations. You'll also get the Green Serpent Brew medicine, which removes status effects, when you visit for the first time.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="15039d1a-d2ec-11f1-8969-7dcbed409bf1" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="15039d1a-d2ec-11f1-8969-7dcbed409bf1" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-crimson-manor-enter" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Crimson Manor</strong></a>: Open the door<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ Where to find the Mandate Encampment Outer Gate Key in Phantom Blade Zero ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:2560px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="mcTjpm2bgi8MvWw7T8gddP" name="phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-1" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Encampment key" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/mcTjpm2bgi8MvWw7T8gddP-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="2560" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/mcTjpm2bgi8MvWw7T8gddP-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: S-Game Studios)</span></figcaption></figure><p>The Mandate Encampment Outer Gate Key is one of the most important to find in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a>, since it unlocks an entire region that's otherwise inaccessible.</p><p>Though you find the gate to the Mandate Encampment when you first arrive in the Village of Lu, the key is actually towards the end of the Pangzhen area (the game's 4th region), which you visit in its second chapter.</p><p>Exploring the west side of the town, you'll eventually reach Gu Wangyue, a Chinese opera singer boss. After defeating her, you can drop down the well in her arena, climb the ladder straight ahead, and you'll find the key to the Mandate Encampment on a corpse in the following room surrounded by puppet enemies.</p><p>It's on the main track through Pangzhen, so you'll definitely go through this room—just make sure to pick it up when you do so you can unseal the gate.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="7f5b727e-d2eb-11f1-b4ff-5fe345ddc766" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="7f5b727e-d2eb-11f1-b4ff-5fe345ddc766" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-crimson-manor-enter" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Crimson Manor</strong></a>: Open the door<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ Open the gate and explore this extra region. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">BTjqgfePkGU7ZkLhSNxzEj</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/QYbhxRciTo6KmPg3rnJWdP-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                <category><![CDATA[Action]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Games]]></category>
                                                                                                                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Sean Martin ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rw7hUY3Y2mxZJtwx3ePdwF-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ null ]]></dc:description>
