                                                    </media:content>
                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/QYbhxRciTo6KmPg3rnJWdP-1920-80.jpg" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:2560px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="mcTjpm2bgi8MvWw7T8gddP" name="phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-1" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Encampment key" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/mcTjpm2bgi8MvWw7T8gddP-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="2560" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/mcTjpm2bgi8MvWw7T8gddP-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: S-Game Studios)</span></figcaption></figure><p>The Mandate Encampment Outer Gate Key is one of the most important to find in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a>, since it unlocks an entire region that's otherwise inaccessible.</p><p>Though you find the gate to the Mandate Encampment when you first arrive in the Village of Lu, the key is actually towards the end of the Pangzhen area (the game's 4th region), which you visit in its second chapter.</p><p>Exploring the west side of the town, you'll eventually reach Gu Wangyue, a Chinese opera singer boss. After defeating her, you can drop down the well in her arena, climb the ladder straight ahead, and you'll find the key to the Mandate Encampment on a corpse in the following room surrounded by puppet enemies.</p><p>It's on the main track through Pangzhen, so you'll definitely go through this room—just make sure to pick it up when you do so you can unseal the gate.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="7f5b727e-d2eb-11f1-b4ff-5fe345ddc766" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="7f5b727e-d2eb-11f1-b4ff-5fe345ddc766" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-crimson-manor-enter" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Crimson Manor</strong></a>: Open the door<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ How to enter the Order's underground tavern in Phantom Blade Zero ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/LivRKdUj.html" id="LivRKdUj" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Order's Tavern" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><p>Opening the entrance to the Order's underground tavern in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a> took me longer than I'd like to admit, but it's required to continue progressing through Pangzhen during the Town of Death quest.</p><p>In the wine yard behind the tavern building, Soul will note that the pavilion's floor on the right is hollow—this is where the secret entrance is, so you'll want to head behind the pavilion and smash the big black jar, as in the video above.</p><p>This reveals a crank which will unlock the cellar and let you inside. Similar to Weeping Creek Valley's outpost or the Crimson Forest's Thieves Camp, this is an important location in Pangzhen and a hub for many of the region's sidequests.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="4d572d12-d2ec-11f1-9004-bb27866d7c11" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="4d572d12-d2ec-11f1-9004-bb27866d7c11" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-enter-orders-underground-tavern/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ Find the secret entrance during the Town of Death quest. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">JtEgr2UMPCbZJaztJrM6wW</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/cwmg7gKguGg4aaq8sH6bRV-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                <category><![CDATA[Action]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Games]]></category>
                                                                                                                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Sean Martin ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rw7hUY3Y2mxZJtwx3ePdwF-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ null ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/cwmg7gKguGg4aaq8sH6bRV-1920-80.jpg">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[S-Game Studios]]></media:credit>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:description><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero - Order&#039;s tavern]]></media:description>                                                            <media:text><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero - Order&#039;s tavern]]></media:text>
                                <media:title type="plain"><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero - Order&#039;s tavern]]></media:title>
                                                    </media:content>
                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/cwmg7gKguGg4aaq8sH6bRV-1920-80.jpg" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/LivRKdUj.html" id="LivRKdUj" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Order's Tavern" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><p>Opening the entrance to the Order's underground tavern in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a> took me longer than I'd like to admit, but it's required to continue progressing through Pangzhen during the Town of Death quest.</p><p>In the wine yard behind the tavern building, Soul will note that the pavilion's floor on the right is hollow—this is where the secret entrance is, so you'll want to head behind the pavilion and smash the big black jar, as in the video above.</p><p>This reveals a crank which will unlock the cellar and let you inside. Similar to Weeping Creek Valley's outpost or the Crimson Forest's Thieves Camp, this is an important location in Pangzhen and a hub for many of the region's sidequests.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="4d572d12-d2ec-11f1-9004-bb27866d7c11" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="4d572d12-d2ec-11f1-9004-bb27866d7c11" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ How to fix the Illusory Pipa in Phantom Blade Zero ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <p>The Illusory Pipa is a phantom edge capable of dispelling certain barriers, but also an important story item in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a>, unsealing a special barrier in the north of the Meigu Lake area.</p><p>To craft it, you'll first need to arrive at the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-enter-orders-underground-tavern" target="_blank">Order's underground tavern</a> in Pangzhen, where you'll meet Myst, the third sister who's capable of repairing the instrument once you find its parts. Here's where to get each of them, though be aware they require significant progression through the game:</p><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-illusory-pipa-head"><span>Illusory Pipa Head</span></h2><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1920px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="HWpBUGrroRFqELrfHtK8vb" name="phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-4" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa - Dusk" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/HWpBUGrroRFqELrfHtK8vb-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="1920" height="1080" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/HWpBUGrroRFqELrfHtK8vb-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="caption-text">Dusk is a secret boss you can access by collecting Firefly's Memory Flowers in the Village of Lu </span><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: S-Game Studios)</span></figcaption></figure><p>Defeat the secret boss, Dusk, in the Village of Lu. Find Firefly's Memory Flowers as part of the Secrets at the Heart of the Lake quest to unlock the barrier at the Temple of Blue Fireflies, then drop down to fight him.</p><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-illusory-pipa-strings"><span>Illusory Pipa Strings </span></h2><figure role="gallery"><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/Dsuke25KQtPZwibBkMG3Qn-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa - Opera house" /><figcaption>You're looking for the sunken opera house in south Meigu Lake<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/VjyigjRNdi2tshwVEraW7c-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa strings " /><figcaption>Defeat Yan Qiansui there to get the strings<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure></figure><p>Defeat Yan Qiansui, The Zither Maiden at the sunken opera house in south Meigu Lake, accessible via north Pangzhen after you've defeated the region boss. Collect Yan'er's Memory Flowers floating around the island, with two towards Pangzhen docks, to access it and fight her.</p><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-illusory-pipa-backplate"><span>Illusory Pipa Backplate </span></h2><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:2560px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="C9gHU7iGa5iuSzGHcHHB9c" name="phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-2" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa backplate" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/C9gHU7iGa5iuSzGHcHHB9c-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="2560" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/C9gHU7iGa5iuSzGHcHHB9c-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="caption-text">The backplate is just after the boss at the end of the Mandate Encampment </span><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: S-Game Studios)</span></figcaption></figure><p>Defeat the final boss at the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank">Mandate Encampment</a> and collect it after. You'll need a key found in Pangzhen (details in linked guide) to access this region near the entrance to the Village of Lu. Once inside, fight through the region to the final boss and grab the backplate on a table just after the battle.</p><p>Once you've got all three parts, head back to Myst in Pangzhen and select the relevant dialogue option to repair the Illusory Pipa. Now you can unseal the barrier in the northeast of Meigu Lake.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="c7ac7078-d2eb-11f1-917e-f1d434d0ef6d" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="c7ac7078-d2eb-11f1-917e-f1d434d0ef6d" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-crimson-manor-enter" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Crimson Manor</strong></a>: Open the door</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ Repair The Chord's instrument to dispel the barrier. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">m735kJDEVXRDuiBYux8Axi</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/tyTyHj8JqhYo2MJHvUPcyb-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                <category><![CDATA[Action]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Games]]></category>
                                                                                                                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Sean Martin ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rw7hUY3Y2mxZJtwx3ePdwF-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ null ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/tyTyHj8JqhYo2MJHvUPcyb-1920-80.jpg">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[S-Game Studios]]></media:credit>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:description><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa]]></media:description>                                                            <media:text><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa]]></media:text>
                                <media:title type="plain"><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa]]></media:title>
                                                    </media:content>
                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/tyTyHj8JqhYo2MJHvUPcyb-1920-80.jpg" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <p>The Illusory Pipa is a phantom edge capable of dispelling certain barriers, but also an important story item in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a>, unsealing a special barrier in the north of the Meigu Lake area.</p><p>To craft it, you'll first need to arrive at the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-enter-orders-underground-tavern" target="_blank">Order's underground tavern</a> in Pangzhen, where you'll meet Myst, the third sister who's capable of repairing the instrument once you find its parts. Here's where to get each of them, though be aware they require significant progression through the game:</p><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-illusory-pipa-head"><span>Illusory Pipa Head</span></h2><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1920px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="HWpBUGrroRFqELrfHtK8vb" name="phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-4" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa - Dusk" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/HWpBUGrroRFqELrfHtK8vb-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="1920" height="1080" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/HWpBUGrroRFqELrfHtK8vb-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="caption-text">Dusk is a secret boss you can access by collecting Firefly's Memory Flowers in the Village of Lu </span><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: S-Game Studios)</span></figcaption></figure><p>Defeat the secret boss, Dusk, in the Village of Lu. Find Firefly's Memory Flowers as part of the Secrets at the Heart of the Lake quest to unlock the barrier at the Temple of Blue Fireflies, then drop down to fight him.</p><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-illusory-pipa-strings"><span>Illusory Pipa Strings </span></h2><figure role="gallery"><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/Dsuke25KQtPZwibBkMG3Qn-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa - Opera house" /><figcaption>You're looking for the sunken opera house in south Meigu Lake<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/VjyigjRNdi2tshwVEraW7c-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa strings " /><figcaption>Defeat Yan Qiansui there to get the strings<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure></figure><p>Defeat Yan Qiansui, The Zither Maiden at the sunken opera house in south Meigu Lake, accessible via north Pangzhen after you've defeated the region boss. Collect Yan'er's Memory Flowers floating around the island, with two towards Pangzhen docks, to access it and fight her.</p><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-illusory-pipa-backplate"><span>Illusory Pipa Backplate </span></h2><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:2560px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="C9gHU7iGa5iuSzGHcHHB9c" name="phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-2" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa backplate" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/C9gHU7iGa5iuSzGHcHHB9c-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="2560" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/C9gHU7iGa5iuSzGHcHHB9c-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="caption-text">The backplate is just after the boss at the end of the Mandate Encampment </span><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: S-Game Studios)</span></figcaption></figure><p>Defeat the final boss at the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank">Mandate Encampment</a> and collect it after. You'll need a key found in Pangzhen (details in linked guide) to access this region near the entrance to the Village of Lu. Once inside, fight through the region to the final boss and grab the backplate on a table just after the battle.</p><p>Once you've got all three parts, head back to Myst in Pangzhen and select the relevant dialogue option to repair the Illusory Pipa. Now you can unseal the barrier in the northeast of Meigu Lake.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="c7ac7078-d2eb-11f1-917e-f1d434d0ef6d" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="c7ac7078-d2eb-11f1-917e-f1d434d0ef6d" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-crimson-manor-enter" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Crimson Manor</strong></a>: Open the door</p></div>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ How to enter the Crimson Manor in Phantom Blade Zero ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <figure role="gallery"><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/ePSmFWQpGBDatQfR85hgNb-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Crimson Manor - Portals" /><figcaption>You need to enter three portals around Wulin to open the hanging puppet's eyes<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/J8izgDFNBnPszt2ifTAhNb-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Crimson Manor - Puppet Tongue" /><figcaption>After that, he'll give you his tongue, which unlocks the Crimson Manor<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure></figure><p>Though you find it early on, the Crimson Manor is actually a bit of endgame area in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a> that you'll be able to open later on.</p><p>You need the Puppet's Tongue item to unseal the door, which comes from completing The Herald's Illusion quest, finding three portals into a strange realm with a hanging puppet. Each portal opens an eye—once you have all three, he'll give you his tongue. Here's where to find each portal:</p><ol start="1"><li>The first portal is by the Puppet Testing Grounds bell in the Village of Lu (the game's 3rd region). This is at the end of the area, after you go down the well, though it's basically impossible to miss.</li><li>The second portal is at the end of the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank">Mandate Encampment</a> area after the region boss. You'll need a key from Pangzhen to open the gate to this region near the entrance to the Village of Lu (details in the linked guide).</li><li>The third portal is at the end of the Mountain of Imprisonment area, again, after the region boss. To access this area, you need to repair the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank">Illusory Pipa</a> and unlock the barrier in the northeast of Meigu Lake.</li></ol><p>Once you head through the third portal, speak to the hanging puppet, and he'll give you his tongue to unlock the Crimson Manor, plus his Yin eye, which is related to another quest. Now, you can get inside the manor and fight the fourth acolyte for the Secrets at the Heart of the Lake quest.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="62b6ff4c-d2e8-11f1-a374-9323775b9f17" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="62b6ff4c-d2e8-11f1-a374-9323775b9f17" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-crimson-manor-enter/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ Find a way into this mysterious red house below the Sha-Chi tower. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">JBjtVdAqEAE5Z2ToW6WUQ3</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/CgpRDoZvX8oeqonXSjQUNb-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                <updated>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:12:40 +0000</updated>
                                                                                                                                            <category><![CDATA[Action]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Games]]></category>
                                                                                                                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Sean Martin ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rw7hUY3Y2mxZJtwx3ePdwF-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ null ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/CgpRDoZvX8oeqonXSjQUNb-1920-80.jpg">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[S-Game Studios]]></media:credit>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:description><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Crimson Manor]]></media:description>                                                            <media:text><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Crimson Manor]]></media:text>
                                <media:title type="plain"><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Crimson Manor]]></media:title>
                                                    </media:content>
                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/CgpRDoZvX8oeqonXSjQUNb-1920-80.jpg" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <figure role="gallery"><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/ePSmFWQpGBDatQfR85hgNb-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Crimson Manor - Portals" /><figcaption>You need to enter three portals around Wulin to open the hanging puppet's eyes<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/J8izgDFNBnPszt2ifTAhNb-1920-80.jpg" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Crimson Manor - Puppet Tongue" /><figcaption>After that, he'll give you his tongue, which unlocks the Crimson Manor<small role="credit">S-Game Studios</small></figcaption></figure></figure><p>Though you find it early on, the Crimson Manor is actually a bit of endgame area in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a> that you'll be able to open later on.</p><p>You need the Puppet's Tongue item to unseal the door, which comes from completing The Herald's Illusion quest, finding three portals into a strange realm with a hanging puppet. Each portal opens an eye—once you have all three, he'll give you his tongue. Here's where to find each portal:</p><ol start="1"><li>The first portal is by the Puppet Testing Grounds bell in the Village of Lu (the game's 3rd region). This is at the end of the area, after you go down the well, though it's basically impossible to miss.</li><li>The second portal is at the end of the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank">Mandate Encampment</a> area after the region boss. You'll need a key from Pangzhen to open the gate to this region near the entrance to the Village of Lu (details in the linked guide).</li><li>The third portal is at the end of the Mountain of Imprisonment area, again, after the region boss. To access this area, you need to repair the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank">Illusory Pipa</a> and unlock the barrier in the northeast of Meigu Lake.</li></ol><p>Once you head through the third portal, speak to the hanging puppet, and he'll give you his tongue to unlock the Crimson Manor, plus his Yin eye, which is related to another quest. Now, you can get inside the manor and fight the fourth acolyte for the Secrets at the Heart of the Lake quest.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="62b6ff4c-d2e8-11f1-a374-9323775b9f17" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="62b6ff4c-d2e8-11f1-a374-9323775b9f17" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ All Quickhand's Request treasure locations in Phantom Blade Zero ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <p>You first meet Quickhand Zhang in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a>'s Crimson Forest and, assuming you free him, arriving at the Thieves Camp and his first hideout, he quickly recruits you to find his counterparts and unmarked treasure in each region.</p><p>I've included videos below of where to find Zhang's hideout and the jade treasure chest locations in each region, plus corresponding text entries that explain what you'll need to do to reach each in terms of battling enemies or grabbing any keys required.</p><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-crimson-forest-treasure-locations"><span>Crimson Forest treasure locations  </span></h2><iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/X4nO0lLJ.html" id="X4nO0lLJ" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Zhang's Treasures (Crimson Forest)" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><ul><li><strong>Reward</strong>: Flying Dagger (Phantom Edge) - Thrown knives that apply poison buildup.</li></ul><ol start="1"><li>From the Outlaw Trap bell, head into the cave directly behind you with the butcher and the dogs to grab the Crimson Forest Tunnel Crank. Use it to unlock the grate in the floor near the bell, drop down, descend the ladder, cross the wooden bridge and defeat the second butcher and dogs, then take the left path up a slope to where you'll find the chest.</li></ol><ol start="2"><li>This second chest is behind the locked Thieves Camp Dungeon gate. To get the key, progress through the Crimson Forest until you arrive at the Cliffside Lodge. Head upstairs to grab the cellar crank, unlock the cellar, then drop down to where you can spot the corpse with the glowing item (the key) below you. Unlock the gate back in the Thieves Camp to find the chest immediately on your right.</li></ol><ol start="3"><li>The third chest is in a cave near the Thieves Camp bell. Exit the camp via the path heading towards Zhang's Hideout, follow the path down around the cliffside into the cave, then fight past the dogs and their master to find the jade chest on your left.</li></ol><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-village-of-lu-treasure-locations"><span>Village of Lu treasure locations</span></h2><iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/I3IJrVGJ.html" id="I3IJrVGJ" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Zhang's Treasures (Village Of Lu)" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><ul><li><strong>Reward</strong>: Fine Thread (accessory) - Increases the damage and Sha-Chi depletion of summoned objects by 50%.</li></ul><ol start="1"><li>From the Well of the Three Puppets bell, head up the stairs to the big house at the very top with the mother puppet who attacks you in the entrance. Turn left, climb the ladder, open the door, and pass through the creepy puppet room to find the chest to the left of the altar at the end.</li></ol><ol start="2"><li>Close to the Lady's Grounds bell, which unlocks after you defeat Master Bi Yuan of the Tianxuan Sect. Head right out of the courtyard, climb the wall to your left, and circle around onto the upper level of the Lady's Grounds where you'll find the chest.</li></ol><ol start="3"><li>From the Survivors' Courtyard bell, head left out of the entrance, go down the stairs, then descend the rope down the shaft to your right. The room at the bottom is filled with puppet enemies, but also the third jade chest.</li></ol><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-pangzhen-treasure-locations"><span>Pangzhen treasure locations</span></h2><iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/DZ2vOxIB.html" id="DZ2vOxIB" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Zhang's Treasures (Pangzheng)" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><ul><li><strong>Reward</strong>: Goldblaze (Phantom Edge): Essentially a rifle.</li></ul><ol start="1"><li>You'll need the Tianxeng Pavillion Key for this first one, which you get by talking to the puppet in the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-enter-orders-underground-tavern" target="_blank">Order's underground tavern</a> to start the Star Performer quest. From the Huang Manor Crossroads, head west down the road with the hanging lanterns and turn left to find the door to Tianxeng Pavillion. Unlock it, taking care of the puppet enemies inside, then take the left staircase to the first floor, and circle around the balcony to find the jade chest in the room at the back.</li></ol><ol start="2"><li>For this one, you'll need the You Loong's Deluge Phantom Edge, which you get by defeating You Loong, Leader of the Blackwater Crew in the pond near the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-banyans-heart-location">Banyan Tree</a> in the far west of Pangzheng. From the Marketplace bell, use the deluge to put out the nearby flaming barrier, head inside, turn right, use the hunter sickle to get up on the rooftops and you'll find a jade chest on a platform just up ahead.</li></ol><ol start="3"><li>From the Backstreet Archway bell at the start of Pangzhen's western section, defeat Wu Xuan, The Fallen General boss, then head through the circular gate behind him and up the stairs to find the chest in a small house at the far end of the garden filled with puppet enemies.</li></ol><ol start="4"><li>From the Pond of Fading Song bell just before the well where you fight Gu Wanyue, The Wailing Wraith, backtrack along the street to just before the pool, and turn right up a set of stairs, through an archway, into a building where you'll find the final jade chest for this region.</li></ol><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-meigu-lake-treasure-locations"><span>Meigu Lake treasure locations</span></h2><iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/pFo863Ka.html" id="pFo863Ka" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Zhang's Treasures (Meigu Lake)" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><ul><li><strong>Reward</strong>: Sha-Chi Blood Catalyst (medicine) - Increases Sha-Chi combo damage by 20% for 15 seconds and restores 20% HP, but ignites you.</li></ul><ol start="1"><li>From the Blackwater Crew Dock bell, on the northern island in the lake, head through the arena where you fought You Loong, The Frenzied Blackwater Crew Leader, out the right side via the ramp, then immediately through the house on your right towards a zipline you'll spot ahead of you. Ride this down, hop over the poles, and turn right onto the sand where the chest is located.</li></ol><ol start="2"><li>The second two treasures in Meigu Lake require you to unlock a special area via the Secrets at the Heart of the Lake quest. In the northwest of Meigu Lake, you'll find a snowy area with a mirror which can only be unsealed by defeating the four acolyte scarecrow bosses around Wulin, including one in the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-crimson-manor-enter" target="_blank">Crimson Manor</a>, which you'll have to fix the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank">Illusory Pipa</a> to ultimately access. It's quite elaborate, but once you're through the mirror, continue through the area until the second bell, then make your way along the cliffside coffins to find the jade chest on a platform at the end.</li></ol><ol start="3"><li>I didn't include this final chest in the video because I didn't want to spoil the area, but it's on your main track through the secret region mentioned above, towards the end of the section where you're navigating across ships. The chest is on the final ship, just before the shrine to the lady that teleports you and is almost impossible to miss.</li></ol><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-mirage-estate-treasure-locations"><span>Mirage Estate treasure locations</span></h2><iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/aMUYQtgH.html" id="aMUYQtgH" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Zhang's Treasures (Mirage Estate)" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><ul><li><strong>Reward</strong>: Thundermoon Lantern (accessory) - Inflicting Thunderstrike on an enemy automatically triggers lightning strikes on enemies in a certain radius.</li></ul><p>An important note before you find these: the Mirage Estate is one of the final areas in the game, so unless you want spoilers, please don't watch the video. Another note: <strong>you have to get the second treasure chest in the Opera House on your first run through</strong>. I'm unsure if this is a bug, but the Opera House door will lock after you've activated the opera and come out the other side, so there's no way back to it. </p><ol start="1"><li>From the Training Grounds bell, pass through the arena where you fought Yuding and out the other side into the courtyard and straight ahead inside the house that the herald appears on the upper floor of. Turn right just inside the entrance to find the chest in a room there.</li></ol><ol start="2"><li>From the Opera House bell, find this chest through the Opera House main gate you unlock once you have the Opera Ticket item, on the left side of the first room. It's very important that you grab this on your first time through the building, as the main gate seems to lock again after you watch the opera and come out the other side.</li></ol><ol start="3"><li>Just after you unlock the secret passage in Leng Tu's Study on the main track, by the Perfect Vessel Estate bell. The chest is just behind the big sculpture in the centre of the room.</li></ol><p>And that's every treasure for Quickhand Zhang, completing his quest.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="0d6444f2-d2eb-11f1-ae79-b96d83624eb2" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="0d6444f2-d2eb-11f1-ae79-b96d83624eb2" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-crimson-manor-enter" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Crimson Manor</strong></a>: Open the door<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ Plus where to find Zhang's hideouts for The Wily Hare's Three Dens quest. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">ps9pfAZ9QptPMfgRaknHq3</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/m6iEeygEB28Tgbu3BzNo8J-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                <updated>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 02:14:24 +0000</updated>
                                                                                                                                            <category><![CDATA[Action]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Games]]></category>
                                                                                                                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Sean Martin ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rw7hUY3Y2mxZJtwx3ePdwF-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ null ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/m6iEeygEB28Tgbu3BzNo8J-1920-80.jpg">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[S-Game Studios]]></media:credit>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:description><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Quickhand Zhang]]></media:description>                                                            <media:text><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Quickhand Zhang]]></media:text>
                                <media:title type="plain"><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Quickhand Zhang]]></media:title>
                                                    </media:content>
                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/m6iEeygEB28Tgbu3BzNo8J-1920-80.jpg" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <p>You first meet Quickhand Zhang in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a>'s Crimson Forest and, assuming you free him, arriving at the Thieves Camp and his first hideout, he quickly recruits you to find his counterparts and unmarked treasure in each region.</p><p>I've included videos below of where to find Zhang's hideout and the jade treasure chest locations in each region, plus corresponding text entries that explain what you'll need to do to reach each in terms of battling enemies or grabbing any keys required.</p><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-crimson-forest-treasure-locations"><span>Crimson Forest treasure locations  </span></h2><iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/X4nO0lLJ.html" id="X4nO0lLJ" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Zhang's Treasures (Crimson Forest)" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><ul><li><strong>Reward</strong>: Flying Dagger (Phantom Edge) - Thrown knives that apply poison buildup.</li></ul><ol start="1"><li>From the Outlaw Trap bell, head into the cave directly behind you with the butcher and the dogs to grab the Crimson Forest Tunnel Crank. Use it to unlock the grate in the floor near the bell, drop down, descend the ladder, cross the wooden bridge and defeat the second butcher and dogs, then take the left path up a slope to where you'll find the chest.</li></ol><ol start="2"><li>This second chest is behind the locked Thieves Camp Dungeon gate. To get the key, progress through the Crimson Forest until you arrive at the Cliffside Lodge. Head upstairs to grab the cellar crank, unlock the cellar, then drop down to where you can spot the corpse with the glowing item (the key) below you. Unlock the gate back in the Thieves Camp to find the chest immediately on your right.</li></ol><ol start="3"><li>The third chest is in a cave near the Thieves Camp bell. Exit the camp via the path heading towards Zhang's Hideout, follow the path down around the cliffside into the cave, then fight past the dogs and their master to find the jade chest on your left.</li></ol><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-village-of-lu-treasure-locations"><span>Village of Lu treasure locations</span></h2><iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/I3IJrVGJ.html" id="I3IJrVGJ" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Zhang's Treasures (Village Of Lu)" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><ul><li><strong>Reward</strong>: Fine Thread (accessory) - Increases the damage and Sha-Chi depletion of summoned objects by 50%.</li></ul><ol start="1"><li>From the Well of the Three Puppets bell, head up the stairs to the big house at the very top with the mother puppet who attacks you in the entrance. Turn left, climb the ladder, open the door, and pass through the creepy puppet room to find the chest to the left of the altar at the end.</li></ol><ol start="2"><li>Close to the Lady's Grounds bell, which unlocks after you defeat Master Bi Yuan of the Tianxuan Sect. Head right out of the courtyard, climb the wall to your left, and circle around onto the upper level of the Lady's Grounds where you'll find the chest.</li></ol><ol start="3"><li>From the Survivors' Courtyard bell, head left out of the entrance, go down the stairs, then descend the rope down the shaft to your right. The room at the bottom is filled with puppet enemies, but also the third jade chest.</li></ol><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-pangzhen-treasure-locations"><span>Pangzhen treasure locations</span></h2><iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/DZ2vOxIB.html" id="DZ2vOxIB" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Zhang's Treasures (Pangzheng)" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><ul><li><strong>Reward</strong>: Goldblaze (Phantom Edge): Essentially a rifle.</li></ul><ol start="1"><li>You'll need the Tianxeng Pavillion Key for this first one, which you get by talking to the puppet in the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-enter-orders-underground-tavern" target="_blank">Order's underground tavern</a> to start the Star Performer quest. From the Huang Manor Crossroads, head west down the road with the hanging lanterns and turn left to find the door to Tianxeng Pavillion. Unlock it, taking care of the puppet enemies inside, then take the left staircase to the first floor, and circle around the balcony to find the jade chest in the room at the back.</li></ol><ol start="2"><li>For this one, you'll need the You Loong's Deluge Phantom Edge, which you get by defeating You Loong, Leader of the Blackwater Crew in the pond near the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-banyans-heart-location">Banyan Tree</a> in the far west of Pangzheng. From the Marketplace bell, use the deluge to put out the nearby flaming barrier, head inside, turn right, use the hunter sickle to get up on the rooftops and you'll find a jade chest on a platform just up ahead.</li></ol><ol start="3"><li>From the Backstreet Archway bell at the start of Pangzhen's western section, defeat Wu Xuan, The Fallen General boss, then head through the circular gate behind him and up the stairs to find the chest in a small house at the far end of the garden filled with puppet enemies.</li></ol><ol start="4"><li>From the Pond of Fading Song bell just before the well where you fight Gu Wanyue, The Wailing Wraith, backtrack along the street to just before the pool, and turn right up a set of stairs, through an archway, into a building where you'll find the final jade chest for this region.</li></ol><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-meigu-lake-treasure-locations"><span>Meigu Lake treasure locations</span></h2><iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/pFo863Ka.html" id="pFo863Ka" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Zhang's Treasures (Meigu Lake)" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><ul><li><strong>Reward</strong>: Sha-Chi Blood Catalyst (medicine) - Increases Sha-Chi combo damage by 20% for 15 seconds and restores 20% HP, but ignites you.</li></ul><ol start="1"><li>From the Blackwater Crew Dock bell, on the northern island in the lake, head through the arena where you fought You Loong, The Frenzied Blackwater Crew Leader, out the right side via the ramp, then immediately through the house on your right towards a zipline you'll spot ahead of you. Ride this down, hop over the poles, and turn right onto the sand where the chest is located.</li></ol><ol start="2"><li>The second two treasures in Meigu Lake require you to unlock a special area via the Secrets at the Heart of the Lake quest. In the northwest of Meigu Lake, you'll find a snowy area with a mirror which can only be unsealed by defeating the four acolyte scarecrow bosses around Wulin, including one in the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-crimson-manor-enter" target="_blank">Crimson Manor</a>, which you'll have to fix the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank">Illusory Pipa</a> to ultimately access. It's quite elaborate, but once you're through the mirror, continue through the area until the second bell, then make your way along the cliffside coffins to find the jade chest on a platform at the end.</li></ol><ol start="3"><li>I didn't include this final chest in the video because I didn't want to spoil the area, but it's on your main track through the secret region mentioned above, towards the end of the section where you're navigating across ships. The chest is on the final ship, just before the shrine to the lady that teleports you and is almost impossible to miss.</li></ol><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-mirage-estate-treasure-locations"><span>Mirage Estate treasure locations</span></h2><iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/aMUYQtgH.html" id="aMUYQtgH" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Zhang's Treasures (Mirage Estate)" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><ul><li><strong>Reward</strong>: Thundermoon Lantern (accessory) - Inflicting Thunderstrike on an enemy automatically triggers lightning strikes on enemies in a certain radius.</li></ul><p>An important note before you find these: the Mirage Estate is one of the final areas in the game, so unless you want spoilers, please don't watch the video. Another note: <strong>you have to get the second treasure chest in the Opera House on your first run through</strong>. I'm unsure if this is a bug, but the Opera House door will lock after you've activated the opera and come out the other side, so there's no way back to it. </p><ol start="1"><li>From the Training Grounds bell, pass through the arena where you fought Yuding and out the other side into the courtyard and straight ahead inside the house that the herald appears on the upper floor of. Turn right just inside the entrance to find the chest in a room there.</li></ol><ol start="2"><li>From the Opera House bell, find this chest through the Opera House main gate you unlock once you have the Opera Ticket item, on the left side of the first room. It's very important that you grab this on your first time through the building, as the main gate seems to lock again after you watch the opera and come out the other side.</li></ol><ol start="3"><li>Just after you unlock the secret passage in Leng Tu's Study on the main track, by the Perfect Vessel Estate bell. The chest is just behind the big sculpture in the centre of the room.</li></ol><p>And that's every treasure for Quickhand Zhang, completing his quest.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="0d6444f2-d2eb-11f1-ae79-b96d83624eb2" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="0d6444f2-d2eb-11f1-ae79-b96d83624eb2" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-crimson-manor-enter" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Crimson Manor</strong></a>: Open the door<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ How to beat the Aberrant Three-Faced Puppet in Phantom Blade Zero ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/VkEoQd4k.html" id="VkEoQd4k" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Aberrant Three-Faced Puppet" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><p>The Aberrant Three-Faced Puppet is the first optional boss you can encounter in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a>, but it's definitely not one you're supposed to beat when you first find it.</p><p>It's definitely possible, but with no Phantom Edges and only your un-upgraded starting weapon, you don't deal anywhere near enough damage to be likely to defeat her, and won't for a while. Here are some tips that'll help you best her when you're ready:</p><ul><li><strong>Return later</strong>: There's no rush to defeat this boss or complete the Triple Threat quest. Defeating her doesn't give you a weapon or anything that's useful in the early game, either, so there's really no reason to bang your head against the fight. To beat her when you first meet her, you basically have to no-hit the entire thing, so it's not really worth it. As you can see in the video above, I returned later in the game and the fight was much more manageable.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Upgrade your weapon and polish your accessories</strong>: In particular, I recommend the Ancient Armor Fragment, Jewel's Knot, and Resonance Talisman for increased damage negation, HP, and Sha-Chi. Also upgrade your weapon—remember you can buy extra materials from vendors. Upgrading your weapon will also unlock new useful skills and ways to deal damage.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Use the Livingwood Talisman to inflict bleed on her</strong>: Puppet bodies aren't susceptible to bleed, but if you grab the Livingwood Talisman in a chest near the Smuggler's Tunnel in the Village of Lu and polish it, you'll deal bleed at 70% effectiveness to the boss with a weapon like <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-best-weapon-jagged-steel" target="_blank">Jagged Steel</a>, doing some bonus damage.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Dodge her smoky black attacks</strong>: These drain your stamina fully if you try to block them, so dodge. Luckily, she doesn't have too many red or blue attacks to dodge counter or parry counter, respectively, which makes things easier.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Always be attacking</strong>: Your regular attacks don't cost stamina, but they do still deal damage and deplete her Sha-Chi over time, so keep up the aggression, blocking her attacks between yours. When her Sha-Chi is broken, spend stamina on Sha-Chi combos to deal proper damage, and don't forget your LT attack when your weapon is powered up.</li></ul><p>After you complete the fight, you'll get the Three-Headed Doll story item, though the next stage of the quest isn't until one of the final areas of the game, so I'd suggest coming back later to check this guide if you're still unsure.</p><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-triple-threat-part-two-late-game-spoilers"><span>Triple-Threat part two (late-game spoilers)</span></h2><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:2560px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="CunR7N8VUH9VwhAbuJUpnR" name="phantom-blade-zero-aberrant-three-faced-puppet" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Triple-Threat - Memory Flower" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/CunR7N8VUH9VwhAbuJUpnR-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="2560" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/CunR7N8VUH9VwhAbuJUpnR-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: S-Game Studios)</span></figcaption></figure><p>After you arrive in the Mirage Estate in Pangzhen (towards the end of the game), you'll eventually find a Memory Flower near to the Training Grounds bell, off to the right side of Yuding's arena. This will trigger the next stage of Triple-Threat, in which you have to find three Memory Flowers marked on your map in the estate. </p><p>You'll then be directed to return to the Crimson Forest, which has now partially frozen over due to the Frost Mask, but before you face this puppet boss again,<strong> you need the Soul Tempered version of Sanguine Reach to defeat them</strong>, which requires the Roaring Flames item:</p><ol start="1"><li>The first part comes from defeating Zhu Yuan, The Searing Blade below the Pangzhen Sha-Chi Tower. You get to this by entering Meigu Lake, accessible via north Pangzhen, then continuing north along the shore, before using the exploding enemy to blow up the barrier leading to the lift, similar to how you access the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-crimson-manor-enter" target="_blank">Crimson Manor</a> area.</li><li>The second comes from completing the third Long Pillar challenge in east Meigu Lake.</li></ol><p>Once you have both of these, you can Soul Temper Sanguine Reach into Blazing Edge after you've met Myst at the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-enter-orders-underground-tavern" target="_blank">Order's underground tavern</a> in Pangzhen, which you already will have at this point. </p><iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/0NjxOnAu.html" id="0NjxOnAu" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Yucong, Twisted Puppet" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><p>Now you can return to the Crimson Forest's Mirrorwood, progress through the area a second time towards where you found the region boss originally (there are new bells, enemies, and chests), then face Yucong, No.34 Twisted Puppet. As my 13 minute video above will attest, this is the longest and trickiest optional fight I've found in the game, so I'd suggest:</p><ul><li><strong>Upgrade Blazing Edge fully</strong>: This is your main method of dealing damage to them and they have a lot of health.</li><li><strong>Fire Meteor is really good</strong>: As you can also see in the video, fully upgraded Fire Meteor is very efficient on a spark-to-damage ratio and since it's fire, is good against puppets.</li><li><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-upgrade-medicine" target="_blank"><strong>Upgrade your medicine</strong></a>: I used Kuye Dew and Merciful Dew since they're so HP efficient (even if the restoration is gradual), and Kuye grants damage negation which stacks incredibly well alongside the Ancient Armor Fragment accessory.</li><li><strong>Use the LT charge on Blazing Edge</strong>: This is especially strong in the section of the fight where you face three separate entities, as you can deal with one of them quickly. The Chaos Mask tends to be the most aggressive, and Frost Mask the most defensive.</li></ul><p>Beyond that, you'll just want plenty of health and Sha-Chi. My other accessories were Talisman of Despair, which increases damage when you haven't attacked for four seconds, up to 35%, so perfect for Blazing Edge's nuke attack. Then Jewel's Knot and Resonance Talisman for more HP and Sha-Chi, then Battleforged, which negates an instance of damage every six seconds you aren't hit.</p><p>Defeat the boss and you'll get their extremely fun Freezing Chaos sword, which can inflict frost or chaos fire. You'll also get the second Chaos Dagger fragment to Soul Temper Sanguine Twin. The other drops from the fourth Long Pillar challenge past the mirror in north Meigu Lake, in case you haven't located it yet.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="a4e44804-d2e6-11f1-9ca3-a96f3afa78da" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="a4e44804-d2e6-11f1-9ca3-a96f3afa78da" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-aberrant-three-faced-puppet-triple-threat/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ Defeat this tricky boss and complete the second part of the Triple-Threat quest. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">LUu7bMEco8TBU3iwers3R</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/UrqQhh73ADzwnUW9GdzXj6-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                <updated>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 02:50:18 +0000</updated>
                                                                                                                                            <category><![CDATA[Action]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Games]]></category>
                                                                                                                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Sean Martin ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rw7hUY3Y2mxZJtwx3ePdwF-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ null ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/UrqQhh73ADzwnUW9GdzXj6-1920-80.jpg">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[S-Game Studios]]></media:credit>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:description><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Aberrant Three-Faced Puppet]]></media:description>                                                            <media:text><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Aberrant Three-Faced Puppet]]></media:text>
                                <media:title type="plain"><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Aberrant Three-Faced Puppet]]></media:title>
                                                    </media:content>
                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/UrqQhh73ADzwnUW9GdzXj6-1920-80.jpg" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/VkEoQd4k.html" id="VkEoQd4k" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Aberrant Three-Faced Puppet" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><p>The Aberrant Three-Faced Puppet is the first optional boss you can encounter in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a>, but it's definitely not one you're supposed to beat when you first find it.</p><p>It's definitely possible, but with no Phantom Edges and only your un-upgraded starting weapon, you don't deal anywhere near enough damage to be likely to defeat her, and won't for a while. Here are some tips that'll help you best her when you're ready:</p><ul><li><strong>Return later</strong>: There's no rush to defeat this boss or complete the Triple Threat quest. Defeating her doesn't give you a weapon or anything that's useful in the early game, either, so there's really no reason to bang your head against the fight. To beat her when you first meet her, you basically have to no-hit the entire thing, so it's not really worth it. As you can see in the video above, I returned later in the game and the fight was much more manageable.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Upgrade your weapon and polish your accessories</strong>: In particular, I recommend the Ancient Armor Fragment, Jewel's Knot, and Resonance Talisman for increased damage negation, HP, and Sha-Chi. Also upgrade your weapon—remember you can buy extra materials from vendors. Upgrading your weapon will also unlock new useful skills and ways to deal damage.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Use the Livingwood Talisman to inflict bleed on her</strong>: Puppet bodies aren't susceptible to bleed, but if you grab the Livingwood Talisman in a chest near the Smuggler's Tunnel in the Village of Lu and polish it, you'll deal bleed at 70% effectiveness to the boss with a weapon like <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-best-weapon-jagged-steel" target="_blank">Jagged Steel</a>, doing some bonus damage.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Dodge her smoky black attacks</strong>: These drain your stamina fully if you try to block them, so dodge. Luckily, she doesn't have too many red or blue attacks to dodge counter or parry counter, respectively, which makes things easier.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Always be attacking</strong>: Your regular attacks don't cost stamina, but they do still deal damage and deplete her Sha-Chi over time, so keep up the aggression, blocking her attacks between yours. When her Sha-Chi is broken, spend stamina on Sha-Chi combos to deal proper damage, and don't forget your LT attack when your weapon is powered up.</li></ul><p>After you complete the fight, you'll get the Three-Headed Doll story item, though the next stage of the quest isn't until one of the final areas of the game, so I'd suggest coming back later to check this guide if you're still unsure.</p><h2 class="article-body__section" id="section-triple-threat-part-two-late-game-spoilers"><span>Triple-Threat part two (late-game spoilers)</span></h2><figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:2560px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="CunR7N8VUH9VwhAbuJUpnR" name="phantom-blade-zero-aberrant-three-faced-puppet" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Triple-Threat - Memory Flower" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/CunR7N8VUH9VwhAbuJUpnR-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="2560" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/CunR7N8VUH9VwhAbuJUpnR-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: S-Game Studios)</span></figcaption></figure><p>After you arrive in the Mirage Estate in Pangzhen (towards the end of the game), you'll eventually find a Memory Flower near to the Training Grounds bell, off to the right side of Yuding's arena. This will trigger the next stage of Triple-Threat, in which you have to find three Memory Flowers marked on your map in the estate. </p><p>You'll then be directed to return to the Crimson Forest, which has now partially frozen over due to the Frost Mask, but before you face this puppet boss again,<strong> you need the Soul Tempered version of Sanguine Reach to defeat them</strong>, which requires the Roaring Flames item:</p><ol start="1"><li>The first part comes from defeating Zhu Yuan, The Searing Blade below the Pangzhen Sha-Chi Tower. You get to this by entering Meigu Lake, accessible via north Pangzhen, then continuing north along the shore, before using the exploding enemy to blow up the barrier leading to the lift, similar to how you access the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-crimson-manor-enter" target="_blank">Crimson Manor</a> area.</li><li>The second comes from completing the third Long Pillar challenge in east Meigu Lake.</li></ol><p>Once you have both of these, you can Soul Temper Sanguine Reach into Blazing Edge after you've met Myst at the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-enter-orders-underground-tavern" target="_blank">Order's underground tavern</a> in Pangzhen, which you already will have at this point. </p><iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/0NjxOnAu.html" id="0NjxOnAu" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Yucong, Twisted Puppet" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><p>Now you can return to the Crimson Forest's Mirrorwood, progress through the area a second time towards where you found the region boss originally (there are new bells, enemies, and chests), then face Yucong, No.34 Twisted Puppet. As my 13 minute video above will attest, this is the longest and trickiest optional fight I've found in the game, so I'd suggest:</p><ul><li><strong>Upgrade Blazing Edge fully</strong>: This is your main method of dealing damage to them and they have a lot of health.</li><li><strong>Fire Meteor is really good</strong>: As you can also see in the video, fully upgraded Fire Meteor is very efficient on a spark-to-damage ratio and since it's fire, is good against puppets.</li><li><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-upgrade-medicine" target="_blank"><strong>Upgrade your medicine</strong></a>: I used Kuye Dew and Merciful Dew since they're so HP efficient (even if the restoration is gradual), and Kuye grants damage negation which stacks incredibly well alongside the Ancient Armor Fragment accessory.</li><li><strong>Use the LT charge on Blazing Edge</strong>: This is especially strong in the section of the fight where you face three separate entities, as you can deal with one of them quickly. The Chaos Mask tends to be the most aggressive, and Frost Mask the most defensive.</li></ul><p>Beyond that, you'll just want plenty of health and Sha-Chi. My other accessories were Talisman of Despair, which increases damage when you haven't attacked for four seconds, up to 35%, so perfect for Blazing Edge's nuke attack. Then Jewel's Knot and Resonance Talisman for more HP and Sha-Chi, then Battleforged, which negates an instance of damage every six seconds you aren't hit.</p><p>Defeat the boss and you'll get their extremely fun Freezing Chaos sword, which can inflict frost or chaos fire. You'll also get the second Chaos Dagger fragment to Soul Temper Sanguine Twin. The other drops from the fourth Long Pillar challenge past the mirror in north Meigu Lake, in case you haven't located it yet.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="a4e44804-d2e6-11f1-9ca3-a96f3afa78da" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="a4e44804-d2e6-11f1-9ca3-a96f3afa78da" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ Where to find the Flesh Lily in Phantom Blade Zero ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/P3qmQVzA.html" id="P3qmQVzA" title="Phantom Blade - Flesh Lily Location" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><p>Finding a Flesh Lily for Yu'er is the first sidequest you'll encounter in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a>, but you can't complete it until a few areas and bosses later.</p><p>You can find the Flesh Lily below the Sha-Chi tower, an area you reach after arriving at the outpost and beating Peng Meng. Specifically, it's accessible from the Valley Sha-Chi Tower 1st Floor bell when you arrive at the base of the tower, though you'll have to fight a boss to get it. Follow the video above, or:</p><ol start="1"><li>From the Valley Sha-Chi Tower 1st Floor bell, ascend the stairs and then circle around the right side of the tower.</li><li>Drop down the hole at the back and slide down the long wooden ramp into the cavern filled with red spider lilies.</li><li>Turn left and head up the slope into the lily-filled clearing above.</li></ol><p>When you arrive in the clearing, a cutscene will play, and you'll find yourself fighting Hua, Deadly Betrothed. She's relatively tricky, but this <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-hua-boss-guide" target="_blank">Hua boss guide</a> offers more tips for defeating her, which will get you her powerful Scarlet Wraithblade. You'll also find the Twinned Flesh Lillies item on the corpse by the pavillion where she was standing at the start of the fight.</p><p>After you defeat Peng Meng, Yu'er appears next to Forge at the outpost, so head there to give her the lily to complete this stage of the quest. She'll offer you the other lily as a memento. When you reach the Thieves Camp in the Crimson Forest, you'll encounter Yu'er again, after which, her questline will continue.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="7f73d5ac-d2e7-11f1-9ac1-b7e0fe21aa17" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="7f73d5ac-d2e7-11f1-9ac1-b7e0fe21aa17" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-crimson-manor-enter" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Crimson Manor</strong></a>: Open the door<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ Track down this rare flower to help Yu'er's father. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">arqckcSLdSK3EwTKrzzcvi</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/Fh9kdG3PrEvkL7ym66t4UX-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                <category><![CDATA[Action]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Games]]></category>
                                                                                                                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Sean Martin ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rw7hUY3Y2mxZJtwx3ePdwF-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ null ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/Fh9kdG3PrEvkL7ym66t4UX-1920-80.jpg">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[S-Game Studio]]></media:credit>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:description><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero - Yu&#039;er with a Flesh Lily]]></media:description>                                                            <media:text><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero - Yu&#039;er with a Flesh Lily]]></media:text>
                                <media:title type="plain"><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero - Yu&#039;er with a Flesh Lily]]></media:title>
                                                    </media:content>
                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/Fh9kdG3PrEvkL7ym66t4UX-1920-80.jpg" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/P3qmQVzA.html" id="P3qmQVzA" title="Phantom Blade - Flesh Lily Location" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><p>Finding a Flesh Lily for Yu'er is the first sidequest you'll encounter in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a>, but you can't complete it until a few areas and bosses later.</p><p>You can find the Flesh Lily below the Sha-Chi tower, an area you reach after arriving at the outpost and beating Peng Meng. Specifically, it's accessible from the Valley Sha-Chi Tower 1st Floor bell when you arrive at the base of the tower, though you'll have to fight a boss to get it. Follow the video above, or:</p><ol start="1"><li>From the Valley Sha-Chi Tower 1st Floor bell, ascend the stairs and then circle around the right side of the tower.</li><li>Drop down the hole at the back and slide down the long wooden ramp into the cavern filled with red spider lilies.</li><li>Turn left and head up the slope into the lily-filled clearing above.</li></ol><p>When you arrive in the clearing, a cutscene will play, and you'll find yourself fighting Hua, Deadly Betrothed. She's relatively tricky, but this <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-hua-boss-guide" target="_blank">Hua boss guide</a> offers more tips for defeating her, which will get you her powerful Scarlet Wraithblade. You'll also find the Twinned Flesh Lillies item on the corpse by the pavillion where she was standing at the start of the fight.</p><p>After you defeat Peng Meng, Yu'er appears next to Forge at the outpost, so head there to give her the lily to complete this stage of the quest. She'll offer you the other lily as a memento. When you reach the Thieves Camp in the Crimson Forest, you'll encounter Yu'er again, after which, her questline will continue.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="7f73d5ac-d2e7-11f1-9ac1-b7e0fe21aa17" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="7f73d5ac-d2e7-11f1-9ac1-b7e0fe21aa17" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-crimson-manor-enter" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Crimson Manor</strong></a>: Open the door<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ Where to find the Backstreet Courtyard Key in Phantom Blade Zero ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:2560px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="p9tJrtaDDjj6qwUNSfsKsV" name="phantom-blade-zero-backstreet-courtyard-key-2" alt="Phantom Blade Zero Backstreet Courtyard Key" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/p9tJrtaDDjj6qwUNSfsKsV-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="2560" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/p9tJrtaDDjj6qwUNSfsKsV-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: S-Game Studios)</span></figcaption></figure><p>I spent a long time in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a> searching for the Backstreet Courtyard Key, convinced it would unlock the inaccessible area where Old Man Gen's house is located, as well as the third acolyte scarecrow. Turns out, that gate doesn't lead to either.</p><p>If you're searching for that key with that in mind, you instead need to acquire the Flaming Mane phantom edge from the region boss and follow the main quest to repair it with Lei Dang, then use it to burn the barrier by the Pond of Fading Song bell where you fought Gu Wanyue, The Wailing Wraith. This leads around the back and lets you access both quest locations. </p><p>Now, if you're here because you're genuinely interested in the Backstreet Courtyard Key, you won't get it until you reach the Mountain of Imprisonment area. Speak to the couple near the Shrine Outer Gate, complete the Ledger of Atonement quest by finding the ledger in the caves below, and then speak to the woman there to start the Bai Xue quest, getting you the key. The location is mainly relevant to this specific quest and doesn't hold much value beyond it.</p><p>If you're wondering how to reach the Mountain of Imprisonment, you'll need to complete the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank">Illusory Pipa</a> quest first.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="8daf902a-d2ec-11f1-b742-733bd45676a4" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="8daf902a-d2ec-11f1-b742-733bd45676a4" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-backstreet-courtyard-key-location/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ Open the locked door in the backstreets of Pangzhen. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">6DtSuCQRBEQDJ3qzVFsWAL</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/f3tcWcvMjhYcSi5iYTCwqV-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                <category><![CDATA[Action]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Games]]></category>
                                                                                                                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Sean Martin ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rw7hUY3Y2mxZJtwx3ePdwF-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ null ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/f3tcWcvMjhYcSi5iYTCwqV-1920-80.jpg">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[S-Game Studios]]></media:credit>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:description><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Backstreet Courtyard Key gate]]></media:description>                                                            <media:text><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Backstreet Courtyard Key gate]]></media:text>
