                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ Phantom Blade Zero's best weapon might just be the first one you get ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:2560px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="aSbPgEBa5FdJs9XZbCS8vC" name="phantom-blade-zero-best-weapon-1" alt="Phantom Blade Zero best weapon - Jagged Steel" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/aSbPgEBa5FdJs9XZbCS8vC-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="2560" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/aSbPgEBa5FdJs9XZbCS8vC-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: S-Game Studios)</span></figcaption></figure><p>Why is bleed always so strong? I guess the entire concept of dealing damage, but also building a status bar on an enemy that <em>deals even more damage</em> when it reaches full, is a bit OP as ideas go. Anyone who's played Elden Ring for any length of time has likely experienced Reduvia and Rivers of Blood, most likely when Nerijus invaded and wiped out their health bar in the starting area.</p><p>Well, <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a> also has an extremely strong bleed weapon early in the game: Jagged Steel, which you get from the first boss you face (who also happens to be called Jagged Steel). During this boss fight, you'll experience the joys of bleed first hand while trying to block him, but this sword is well worth it:</p><ul><li>Its central weapon mechanic is Blood Blade, a stackable buff that increases bleed buildup and damage.</li><li>At Level 5, it gets a special attack against guard-broken enemies which grants a Blood Blade stack.</li><li>At Level 10 it gets more bleed buildup.</li><li>At Level 15, you can charge a slash to build stacks of Blood Blade before unleashing them.</li><li>At Level 20, it gets <em>even more </em>bleed buildup.</li></ul><p>And this isn't mentioning its powered-up left trigger combo which unleashes a flurry of slashes that rapidly apply bleed buildup, basically a guaranteed bleed proc every time. A significant portion of Phantom Blade Zero's bosses are humans who are all susceptible to bleed, making it very strong early in the game.</p><p>But if you're thinking: surely it's not effective against all enemies? You'd be right. There are Puppets, Golden Bodies, and Phantom Bodies which bleed doesn't work on. Or at least it doesn't until you grab the Livingwood Talisman in the Village of Lu in a chest near the Smuggler's Tunnel, an accessory that makes bleed work on <em>all of the above</em> at 50% effectiveness.</p><p>You can also polish this accessory to improve that to 70%, so now you have a very powerful bleed weapon that can apply it to every enemy and boss in the game at almost full effectiveness. I'm about 30 hours in as I write this and even though I've experimented with various weapons, and have some dual-swords in my second slot, I'm <em>still </em>using Jagged Steel. It's just really damn strong, especially in terms of its offensive skills.</p><p>So, if you're looking for a weapon to make the early game easier in Phantom Blade Zero, invest in Jagged Steel—you won't regret it.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="08c1763c-d2e5-11f1-abad-5d99e6211a8e" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="08c1763c-d2e5-11f1-abad-5d99e6211a8e" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-best-weapon-jagged-steel/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ Bleed's back on the menu, boys. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">t2QpAAta5scMe9xGwS4Bzf</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/7rVNNg3tqanb9juZ9aueEQ-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                <category><![CDATA[Action]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Games]]></category>
                                                                                                                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Sean Martin ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rw7hUY3Y2mxZJtwx3ePdwF-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ null ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/7rVNNg3tqanb9juZ9aueEQ-1920-80.jpg">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[S-Game Studios]]></media:credit>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:description><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero best weapon - Soul]]></media:description>                                                            <media:text><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero best weapon - Soul]]></media:text>
                                <media:title type="plain"><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero best weapon - Soul]]></media:title>
                                                    </media:content>
                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/7rVNNg3tqanb9juZ9aueEQ-1920-80.jpg" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <figure class="van-image-figure  inline-layout" data-bordeaux-image-check="" ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:2560px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="aSbPgEBa5FdJs9XZbCS8vC" name="phantom-blade-zero-best-weapon-1" alt="Phantom Blade Zero best weapon - Jagged Steel" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/aSbPgEBa5FdJs9XZbCS8vC-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="1" width="2560" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" class="inline expandable" /><a href='https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/aSbPgEBa5FdJs9XZbCS8vC-1920-80.jpg' target='_blank' class='expand-button icon-expand-image icon' ></a></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=" inline-layout"><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: S-Game Studios)</span></figcaption></figure><p>Why is bleed always so strong? I guess the entire concept of dealing damage, but also building a status bar on an enemy that <em>deals even more damage</em> when it reaches full, is a bit OP as ideas go. Anyone who's played Elden Ring for any length of time has likely experienced Reduvia and Rivers of Blood, most likely when Nerijus invaded and wiped out their health bar in the starting area.</p><p>Well, <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a> also has an extremely strong bleed weapon early in the game: Jagged Steel, which you get from the first boss you face (who also happens to be called Jagged Steel). During this boss fight, you'll experience the joys of bleed first hand while trying to block him, but this sword is well worth it:</p><ul><li>Its central weapon mechanic is Blood Blade, a stackable buff that increases bleed buildup and damage.</li><li>At Level 5, it gets a special attack against guard-broken enemies which grants a Blood Blade stack.</li><li>At Level 10 it gets more bleed buildup.</li><li>At Level 15, you can charge a slash to build stacks of Blood Blade before unleashing them.</li><li>At Level 20, it gets <em>even more </em>bleed buildup.</li></ul><p>And this isn't mentioning its powered-up left trigger combo which unleashes a flurry of slashes that rapidly apply bleed buildup, basically a guaranteed bleed proc every time. A significant portion of Phantom Blade Zero's bosses are humans who are all susceptible to bleed, making it very strong early in the game.</p><p>But if you're thinking: surely it's not effective against all enemies? You'd be right. There are Puppets, Golden Bodies, and Phantom Bodies which bleed doesn't work on. Or at least it doesn't until you grab the Livingwood Talisman in the Village of Lu in a chest near the Smuggler's Tunnel, an accessory that makes bleed work on <em>all of the above</em> at 50% effectiveness.</p><p>You can also polish this accessory to improve that to 70%, so now you have a very powerful bleed weapon that can apply it to every enemy and boss in the game at almost full effectiveness. I'm about 30 hours in as I write this and even though I've experimented with various weapons, and have some dual-swords in my second slot, I'm <em>still </em>using Jagged Steel. It's just really damn strong, especially in terms of its offensive skills.</p><p>So, if you're looking for a weapon to make the early game easier in Phantom Blade Zero, invest in Jagged Steel—you won't regret it.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="08c1763c-d2e5-11f1-abad-5d99e6211a8e" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="08c1763c-d2e5-11f1-abad-5d99e6211a8e" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ How to complete Whence the Weeping in Phantom Blade Zero ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <p>Whence the Weeping might seem like a sidequest you're supposed to complete in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a>'s first Weeping Creek Valley area, but it's actually a major quest that takes a significant portion of the game to finish. If you've just started and are here wondering if you've missed something: you haven't, and you don't need this guide right now.</p><p>It's also relatively straightforward—it's just that quest tracking isn't available for it until you progress further. I'll run through its steps below, but these will contain spoilers for how to access a later game region, so you might want to steer clear:</p><ol start="1"><li>As you progress through the Crimson Forest (2nd region), you'll hear the weeping again, giving you a nav marker that coincides with the region boss, which provides a few more answers.</li></ol><ol start="2"><li>When you arrive in the Village of Lu (3rd region) and speak to Jewel about the weeping, she speculates that The Chord wants to tell you something, and you're directed to the northeast of Meigu Lake.</li></ol><ol start="3"><li>You'll have to progress through Pangzhen (4th region) and defeat its main boss in the west to get the Phantom Edge that unlocks the way to Meigu Lake via the north of the town.</li></ol><ol start="4"><li>In the northeast of Meigu Lake, you'll find a barrier that only the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank">Illusory Pipa</a> Phantom Edge can dispel—fixing it is a whole quest in itself, so see the linked guide for details.</li></ol><ol start="5"><li>Once fixed, dispel the barrier to enter the Mountain of Imprisonment region, progress to the region boss at the top of the mountain, and defeat it to complete the quest.</li></ol><p>As mentioned, this will require significant progression through the game, but it's relatively straightforward and follows alongside the main track for the most part.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="256782f8-d2e6-11f1-a471-51cc2999cfe8" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="256782f8-d2e6-11f1-a471-51cc2999cfe8" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-whence-the-weeping-walkthrough/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ Find the source of the weeping and discover its mysteries. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">rdMrNMjGuXLu4H6wVzopuK</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/mQhWzkGDcwYPgBFAaGomZW-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
