                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <p>Whence the Weeping might seem like a sidequest you're supposed to complete in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a>'s first Weeping Creek Valley area, but it's actually a major quest that takes a significant portion of the game to finish. If you've just started and are here wondering if you've missed something: you haven't, and you don't need this guide right now.</p><p>It's also relatively straightforward—it's just that quest tracking isn't available for it until you progress further. I'll run through its steps below, but these will contain spoilers for how to access a later game region, so you might want to steer clear:</p><ol start="1"><li>As you progress through the Crimson Forest (2nd region), you'll hear the weeping again, giving you a nav marker that coincides with the region boss, which provides a few more answers.</li></ol><ol start="2"><li>When you arrive in the Village of Lu (3rd region) and speak to Jewel about the weeping, she speculates that The Chord wants to tell you something, and you're directed to the northeast of Meigu Lake.</li></ol><ol start="3"><li>You'll have to progress through Pangzhen (4th region) and defeat its main boss in the west to get the Phantom Edge that unlocks the way to Meigu Lake via the north of the town.</li></ol><ol start="4"><li>In the northeast of Meigu Lake, you'll find a barrier that only the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank">Illusory Pipa</a> Phantom Edge can dispel—fixing it is a whole quest in itself, so see the linked guide for details.</li></ol><ol start="5"><li>Once fixed, dispel the barrier to enter the Mountain of Imprisonment region, progress to the region boss at the top of the mountain, and defeat it to complete the quest.</li></ol><p>As mentioned, this will require significant progression through the game, but it's relatively straightforward and follows alongside the main track for the most part.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="256782f8-d2e6-11f1-a471-51cc2999cfe8" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="256782f8-d2e6-11f1-a471-51cc2999cfe8" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ Where to find The Banyan's Heart in Phantom Blade Zero ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/vmrqYxD2.html" id="vmrqYxD2" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Jing Ye, Banyan Tree" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><p>You'll need The Banyan's Heart in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a> to unlock certain skills like Fluid Form Level 2, Quick Remedy, or Opening Strike.</p><p>You can get your first Banyan Heart towards the end of the Crimson Forest area, just after you activate the Parting Mists bell, after you fight Stone Fist Iron Fever—it's basically impossible to miss:</p><ol start="1"><li>Drop down from the Parting Mists bell and head across to the island with the tree directly ahead of you.</li><li>Interact with it to be transported into The Banyan Tree's trial realm.</li></ol><p>You'll have to defeat three waves of enemies, culminating in Jing Ye, the bleed bandit boss from earlier in the Crimson Forest. Similar to the Long Pillars, if you die, there is a bell you can use, and as with boss phases, if you complete a stage of the trial, it's done and you'll start at the next.</p><p>I genuinely think Jing Ye is the most annoying boss I've encountered so far. I recommend equipping the Cavalrybane accessory you can get in the Crimson Forest for more damage when he's mounted, plus the Shieldbreaker talisman if you found it in the Weeping Creek Valley to break his shield quicker. Other than that:</p><ul><li>Draw him away from the two other enemies who spawn.</li><li>Dodge his bleed projectiles as blocking them still builds bleed.</li><li>Use your Dread Axe Phantom Edge to smash his shield—as soon as he falls off his horse, charge a full one.</li></ul><p>If you're still struggling, I've included my video of the boss above, but remember you can come back later, too. Once you defeat him, you'll get the Banyan Heart. </p><h2 id="all-other-banyan-tree-locations">All other Banyan Tree locations</h2><p>Getting your first Banyan Heart will also start The Heart of the Banyan collectible quest to find four more:</p><ul><li>The second Banyan Tree is in Pangzhen during its second chapter, near the Lion Dance Hall in the northwest.</li><li>The third Banyan Tree is close to the start of the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-outer-gate-key-location" target="_blank">Mandate Encampment</a>.</li><li>The fourth Banyan Tree is on an island in Meigu Lake.</li><li>The final tree is in the Mountain of Imprisonment on the main path through the region, though you'll need the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank">Illusory Pipa</a> to get here.</li></ul><p>You can also buy Banyan Hearts from Quickhand Zhang for 100,000 at his den in the Village of Lu onwards. He seems to get a new heart for each new den you find, though this may be linked to completing his <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank">treasure hunts</a> (which I did).</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="673b00f8-d2e9-11f1-b67c-6d1d9b1323b4" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="673b00f8-d2e9-11f1-b67c-6d1d9b1323b4" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-banyans-heart-location/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ Acquire this special material to unlock new skills. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">TRaNLpaijH9hfnqkoXLUeR</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/N2mf2bj7nLarUx9Xx2vSwj-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                <category><![CDATA[Action]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Games]]></category>
                                                                                                                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Sean Martin ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rw7hUY3Y2mxZJtwx3ePdwF-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ null ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/N2mf2bj7nLarUx9Xx2vSwj-1920-80.jpg">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[S-Game Studios]]></media:credit>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:description><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Banyan Tree]]></media:description>                                                            <media:text><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Banyan Tree]]></media:text>
                                <media:title type="plain"><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Banyan Tree]]></media:title>
                                                    </media:content>
                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/N2mf2bj7nLarUx9Xx2vSwj-1920-80.jpg" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/vmrqYxD2.html" id="vmrqYxD2" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Jing Ye, Banyan Tree" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><p>You'll need The Banyan's Heart in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a> to unlock certain skills like Fluid Form Level 2, Quick Remedy, or Opening Strike.</p><p>You can get your first Banyan Heart towards the end of the Crimson Forest area, just after you activate the Parting Mists bell, after you fight Stone Fist Iron Fever—it's basically impossible to miss:</p><ol start="1"><li>Drop down from the Parting Mists bell and head across to the island with the tree directly ahead of you.</li><li>Interact with it to be transported into The Banyan Tree's trial realm.</li></ol><p>You'll have to defeat three waves of enemies, culminating in Jing Ye, the bleed bandit boss from earlier in the Crimson Forest. Similar to the Long Pillars, if you die, there is a bell you can use, and as with boss phases, if you complete a stage of the trial, it's done and you'll start at the next.</p><p>I genuinely think Jing Ye is the most annoying boss I've encountered so far. I recommend equipping the Cavalrybane accessory you can get in the Crimson Forest for more damage when he's mounted, plus the Shieldbreaker talisman if you found it in the Weeping Creek Valley to break his shield quicker. Other than that:</p><ul><li>Draw him away from the two other enemies who spawn.</li><li>Dodge his bleed projectiles as blocking them still builds bleed.</li><li>Use your Dread Axe Phantom Edge to smash his shield—as soon as he falls off his horse, charge a full one.</li></ul><p>If you're still struggling, I've included my video of the boss above, but remember you can come back later, too. Once you defeat him, you'll get the Banyan Heart. </p><h2 id="all-other-banyan-tree-locations">All other Banyan Tree locations</h2><p>Getting your first Banyan Heart will also start The Heart of the Banyan collectible quest to find four more:</p><ul><li>The second Banyan Tree is in Pangzhen during its second chapter, near the Lion Dance Hall in the northwest.</li><li>The third Banyan Tree is close to the start of the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-outer-gate-key-location" target="_blank">Mandate Encampment</a>.</li><li>The fourth Banyan Tree is on an island in Meigu Lake.</li><li>The final tree is in the Mountain of Imprisonment on the main path through the region, though you'll need the <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank">Illusory Pipa</a> to get here.</li></ul><p>You can also buy Banyan Hearts from Quickhand Zhang for 100,000 at his den in the Village of Lu onwards. He seems to get a new heart for each new den you find, though this may be linked to completing his <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank">treasure hunts</a> (which I did).</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="673b00f8-d2e9-11f1-b67c-6d1d9b1323b4" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="673b00f8-d2e9-11f1-b67c-6d1d9b1323b4" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ How to beat Hua, Deadly Betrothed in Phantom Blade Zero ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/CooIujFT.html" id="CooIujFT" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Hua" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><p>Hua, Deadly Betrothed is one of the first optional bosses in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a>, below the Sha-Chi Tower in the Weeping Creek Valley, but you'll have to defeat her if you want to find a <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank">Flesh Lily</a> for Yu'er.</p><p>The trickiest part of this fight is avoiding Hua's spider lilies, but here are some tips to defeat her, plus a video above of my successful run employing these strategies:</p><ul><li><strong>Avoid her lilies and stay mobile</strong>: There are three types of lily in this fight:<ul><li>Those that bloom periodically and when she attacks, before exploding. </li><li>Those that patrol the arena and explode when they all meet in one spot.</li><li>White lilies she fires out that track and stun you, letting her follow up with a red grab attack. These are the most dangerous, especially as she teleports to attack you after she fires them. Make some distance and either dodge or block them when you're sure she isn't attacking.</li></ul></li></ul><ul><li><strong>Learn to counter her red grabs</strong>: This is Hua's deadliest attack, when she flashes red, grabs you and deals a lot of damage with a decapitating slash. If you're struggling to react, remember, red attacks are right bumper to parry, blue attacks are left, though you can just press both if it's less confusing. Hua also seems to attempt a grab if you get clipped by the red flying lilies, so watch out.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Use the Dread Axe to extend your damage phase</strong>: After you stun Hua, you'll be able to safely damage her for a while, but you can extend your damage phase a bit by charging the Dread Axe Phantom Edge to its first level towards the end (until it pings blue) as this will knock her over.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Prepare yourself</strong>: I recommend upgrading a weapon to Level 5 to unlock its ability. I used <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-best-weapon-jagged-steel" target="_blank">Jagged Steel</a> (though bleed doesn't work on her), so use whatever's comfortable. Remember you can buy more upgrade materials from the outpost merchant. Also, make sure to upgrade your healing art and grab the Focus Pill medicine from the chest up the hill to the left (just after The Axemaster's Holding Cell bell). You'll have to use the axe to smash open the way.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Remember the fundamentals</strong>: You can attack with X without it costing stamina, but when you stun her, you should use Y combos instead for extra damage. When your weapon is charged, remember to use LT to perform a special combo. Also, parry her attacks as much as possible, as this will retain your stamina for attacking, dodging, and blocking.</li></ul><ul><li><strong>Dodge her stamina draining attacks</strong>: She'll occasionally perform a downwards slam where she gives off a smoky black aura—this means her next attack will drain all your stamina, so it's better to dodge, especially as it summons a bunch of lilies which explode afterwards. Dodging, in general, is very useful in this fight.</li></ul><p>It can be a tricky fight early on, but she doesn't have all that many combos, and her blue parriable attacks are quite predictable, coming at the end of her four hit sequence. The real key to this fight is making sure you don't get hit by the lilies by making space and being mindful of the arena, while also countering her deadly red grab attacks.</p><p>Once you beat her, you'll get the Scarlet Wraithblade weapon, which can also summon exploding lilies.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="d49ad1a2-d2e7-11f1-b5d0-c1a45c3d14e8" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="d49ad1a2-d2e7-11f1-b5d0-c1a45c3d14e8" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-hua-boss-guide/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ Defeat this phantom bride below the Valley Sha-Chi tower. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
