                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ How to beat The Gold-Masked One in Phantom Blade Zero ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/gRaYHif5.html" id="gRaYHif5" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Gold-Masked One" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><p>The Gold-Masked One inside the Long Pillar in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a> is a bit of an unconventional boss fight. Each of the pillar fights in the Bloodline Awakening quest is a challenge battle against this boss which teaches you different aspects of the game's combat.</p><p>The first battle is all about parrying, hence why it gives you the tip box in the top right. This fight is tricky because of its main gimmick:</p><ul><li>You can't damage The Gold-Masked One apart from after a parry or perfect dodge (a blue or red attack) or unless his Sha-Chi is broken.</li></ul><p>Usually, in Phantom Blade Zero's boss fights, it pays to attack constantly, especially as regular attacks don't even cost Sha-Chi. But in this fight, your attacks won't do anything. Instead, you should:</p><ol start="1"><li>Counter his red (perfect dodge) or blue (perfect parry) attacks and then attack after that to deplete his Sha-Chi. If you're struggling with reacting and hitting the right or left bumper on controller, just press both.</li><li>When it's depleted, deal as much damage as you can in the duration. I recommend using <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-best-weapon-jagged-steel" target="_blank">Jagged Steel</a> since he's susceptible to bleed.</li><li>Rinse and repeat.</li></ol><p>The video above shows the process, but this fight can be quite tricky early on because he has a lot of health and it's a battle of attrition. Make sure your weapon is as upgraded as much as it can be for the attempt, and have the best accessories you can equipped—I was using Quick Hand Pendant, Ancient Armor Fragment, Jewel's Knot, and Resonance Talisman, for increased one-hand damage, damage negation, HP, and Sha-Chi. But I came back to this fight later after I arrived in Pangzhen. </p><p>There's really no rush to beat The Gold-Masked One. As you progress, you'll get more HP, Sha-Chi, weapon upgrades, and the ability to polish accessories, increasing their buffs, which makes things easier. If you are intent on doing it when you reach it, though, be prepared for a long battle. </p><p>Once done, the reward is the Counterstrike Bracers, which increase damage dealt by 20% for two seconds after a parry, and you can also attempt the second Long Pillar challenge in the Crimson Forest.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="2297eb32-d2e9-11f1-8eea-111b28243796" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="2297eb32-d2e9-11f1-8eea-111b28243796" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-gold-masked-one-boss-guide/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ Complete the Long Pillar challenge. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">TmtV64hvsFtKqRXCrrsqPQ</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/CG76CztHFLMWgYfgyHVBEP-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                <category><![CDATA[Action]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Games]]></category>
                                                                                                                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Sean Martin ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rw7hUY3Y2mxZJtwx3ePdwF-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ null ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/CG76CztHFLMWgYfgyHVBEP-1920-80.jpg">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[S-Game Studios]]></media:credit>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:description><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Gold-Masked One]]></media:description>                                                            <media:text><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Gold-Masked One]]></media:text>
                                <media:title type="plain"><![CDATA[Phantom Blade Zero Gold-Masked One]]></media:title>
                                                    </media:content>
                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/CG76CztHFLMWgYfgyHVBEP-1920-80.jpg" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <iframe src="https://content.jwplatform.com/players/gRaYHif5.html" id="gRaYHif5" title="Phantom Blade Zero - Gold-Masked One" width="1920" height="1080" frameborder="0" scrolling="auto" allowfullscreen=""></iframe><p>The Gold-Masked One inside the Long Pillar in <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/phantom-blade-zero/" target="_blank">Phantom Blade Zero</a> is a bit of an unconventional boss fight. Each of the pillar fights in the Bloodline Awakening quest is a challenge battle against this boss which teaches you different aspects of the game's combat.</p><p>The first battle is all about parrying, hence why it gives you the tip box in the top right. This fight is tricky because of its main gimmick:</p><ul><li>You can't damage The Gold-Masked One apart from after a parry or perfect dodge (a blue or red attack) or unless his Sha-Chi is broken.</li></ul><p>Usually, in Phantom Blade Zero's boss fights, it pays to attack constantly, especially as regular attacks don't even cost Sha-Chi. But in this fight, your attacks won't do anything. Instead, you should:</p><ol start="1"><li>Counter his red (perfect dodge) or blue (perfect parry) attacks and then attack after that to deplete his Sha-Chi. If you're struggling with reacting and hitting the right or left bumper on controller, just press both.</li><li>When it's depleted, deal as much damage as you can in the duration. I recommend using <a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-best-weapon-jagged-steel" target="_blank">Jagged Steel</a> since he's susceptible to bleed.</li><li>Rinse and repeat.</li></ol><p>The video above shows the process, but this fight can be quite tricky early on because he has a lot of health and it's a battle of attrition. Make sure your weapon is as upgraded as much as it can be for the attempt, and have the best accessories you can equipped—I was using Quick Hand Pendant, Ancient Armor Fragment, Jewel's Knot, and Resonance Talisman, for increased one-hand damage, damage negation, HP, and Sha-Chi. But I came back to this fight later after I arrived in Pangzhen. </p><p>There's really no rush to beat The Gold-Masked One. As you progress, you'll get more HP, Sha-Chi, weapon upgrades, and the ability to polish accessories, increasing their buffs, which makes things easier. If you are intent on doing it when you reach it, though, be prepared for a long battle. </p><p>Once done, the reward is the Counterstrike Bracers, which increase damage dealt by 20% for two seconds after a parry, and you can also attempt the second Long Pillar challenge in the Crimson Forest.</p><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="2297eb32-d2e9-11f1-8eea-111b28243796" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:1440px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:100.00%;"><img id="EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z" name="phantom-blade-zero-10" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/EX3dY4pSWNSzFJSLVfr65Z-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="1440" height="1440" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-tips" target="_blank" data-dimension112="2297eb32-d2e9-11f1-8eea-111b28243796" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension48="Phantom Blade Zero tips" data-dimension25=""><strong>Phantom Blade Zero tips</strong></a>: Conquer the Wulin<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-flesh-lily-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Flesh Lily</strong></a>: Find Yu'er's flower<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-quickhand-request-treasure-locations-relics" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Zhang's treasures</strong></a>: Every relic<br /><strong></strong><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-mandate-encampment-key-location" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Mandate Camp Key</strong></a>: Get inside<br /><a href="http://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/phantom-blade-zero-illusory-pipa-walkthrough" target="_blank"><strong>Phantom Blade Zero Illusory Pipa</strong></a>: Repair the lute</p></div>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ GTA 6's NPCs have about 600,000 animations, as well as personality traits that take 'demographic and professional' variables into account ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <p>Grand Theft Auto 6's NPCs are so incredibly complicated, it briefly <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/action/gta-6-was-delayed-partially-because-the-amount-of-npcs-was-horrifying-and-required-a-dedicated-studio-full-of-writers-to-handle/">sent the studio into a bit of a "horrifying"</a> spin, requiring an entire team of writers and producers to be assembled just to handle the workload. This has since been doubly confirmed by the studio in a recent <a href="https://www.gamesradar.com/edge/gtavi-cover/">mega-preview from our friends at Edge</a>:</p><p>"This same philosophy governs the streets," the preview reads, "Rather than relying chiefly on procedural systems to assemble interchangeable crowds, Rockstar established an entire Los Angeles-based team of writers, directors and producers devoted to making Leonida's NPCs more individually realised."</p><p>According to the feature, that meant creating an absurd number of animations: "The studio art-directed every [NPC], creating around 600,000 animations."</p><p>What's more, "these pedestrians are assigned personality traits that help determine how they respond: temperament, aggression, where they are, what they have seen, and how the player has behaved towards them. Different districts have their own demographic and professional textures."</p><p>As for what a "professional texture" actually is, Rockstar North co-studio head Rob Nelson goes into more detail: "Who's going to be aggressive? How many people are going to go for a weapon? How many are going to test me?" Nelson says, repeating the same self affirmations I make daily in the mirror.</p><p>The preview continues: "The old GTA pedestrian, a kind of moving prop waiting to panic when the player points a gun, has here splintered into a kaleidoscopic range of possible reactions. Back on the sidewalk, that abstraction suddenly becomes practical. The man with the dog has decided that Jason's stare constitutes a test. </p><p>"He squares up, then unclips the leash from the animal's collar. Nelson turns and runs. The dog gives chase. A flock of pigeons bursts into the air. Finally, the animal loses interest and trots back to its owner. Jason slows to a walk, selects a pack of cigarettes from his inventory, lights one, takes a drag, and continues down the street."</p><figure role="gallery"><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/T9i3ELY2SbwqjddTenqBxK-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 location Ambrosia" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/rjLFde7bmaQCWqYowbJvaD-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 character Real Dimez" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/YH3iSkA5ibnzmxVCCUR2LZ-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 Vice City screenshot" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/kKdLdoqBqEoLHHRF5ECvGa-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 Vice City screenshot" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/cvwjuWSQa3pRDSHyG2roXo-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 Leonida Keys screenshot" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/WZFiWSGdnEmxuRKVaKB37-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 Leonida Keys screenshot" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure></figure><p>Really, the way the preview puts it, GTA 6 seems so thoroughly complicated you could legitimately just sit there and people-watch for a bit: "On the opposite side of the road, Nelson spots an arrest taking place. A suspect is being cuffed by two police officers, who have left their vehicles unattended. He sneaks up to one, clicks the boot open, pulls out a shotgun and slings it onto his back, before walking on, leaving a puff of cigarette smoke curling in the air. We have been watching for three minutes."</p><p>Is this sort of immersive sim, top-end simulation particularly necessary in a videogame that, in its purest form, is about wildly driving vehicles and committing crimes? If you're Rockstar, clearly it is, and I can't say I'm not impressed by the amount of craft reportedly on display here. We'll see how it all holds up when millions of people are playing.</p><p>On console, that is—we're still waiting to hear about a GTA 6 PC launch date. <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/grand-theft-auto/report-claims-grand-theft-auto-6-will-launch-on-pc-sooner-than-anyone-expected/">Rumor has it</a> that the wait won't be too long, but we're not holding our breath.</p><p>You can read <a href="https://www.gamesradar.com/edge/gtavi-cover/">Edge's GTA 6 feature story over at GamesRadar</a>.</p> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/grand-theft-auto/gta-6s-npcs-have-about-600-000-animations-as-well-as-personality-traits-that-take-demographic-and-professional-variables-into-account/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ "Who's going to be aggressive? … How many are going to test me?" ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">jPYY7i43Fyxtq6iKfi6rzj</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/mGAbwHEYqU99h2xFrdszPL-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:52:16 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                                                                                                                <category><![CDATA[Grand Theft Auto]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Games]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Action]]></category>
                                                                                                <author><![CDATA[ harvey.randall@futurenet.com (Harvey Randall) ]]></author>                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Harvey Randall ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/Rws7mDGqrkaXrNKCH4jZ2D-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ &lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt; ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/mGAbwHEYqU99h2xFrdszPL-1920-80.jpg">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[Rockstar Games]]></media:credit>
