                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ 'I feel like we've built a pyramid on Everest' says Rockstar of GTA 6 meeting impossible expectations ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <p>It is not hyperbole to say that GTA 6 is the most anticipated videogame of all time. That'll happen when one of the most acclaimed game developers of all time takes 13 years to finally put out a new game in one of the most popular series of all time.</p><p>That's a hell of a lot of pressure for the army of developers at Rockstar. In a conversation with our friends at Edge for <a href="https://www.gamesradar.com/edge/gtavi-cover/" target="_blank">the magazine's big inside look at GTA 6</a>, Rockstar North head of development Aaron Garbut spoke about meeting the series' absurd standards.</p><p>"We can't just trot out something that's what people might expect, or that was the easy thing to do," he says. "We've not compromised on the scale, the detail, the interactivity, the story, the open world."</p><p>Despite the studio's famously secretive posture, Garbut says the team is very much aware of the galactic expectations, and deployed an illustrative metaphor to communicate how he thinks they've managed to meet them.</p><p>"I feel like we've built a pyramid on Everest."</p><p>While my mind instantly goes to an eventual GTA 6 mod that'll let me ride a giant pyramid down the biggest mountain in Leonida (will fake Florida have mountains?), I have little reason to doubt Garbut's claims here. Impressions, leaks, and Rockstar's own communications suggest that GTA 6 is doubling down on the systemic details that elevated <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/red-dead-redemption-2-review/">Red Dead Redemption 2</a> from 'GTA with horses' to a crime-forward life sim.</p><p>That game's missions were Rockstar's familiar brand of organized crime, but the things you spent time doing between them were quite new for a mainstream game: Eating, drinking, grooming yourself, camping, browsing, and making small talk with locals. These actions often had some gameplay ramifications, but it was common to perform because it felt like the human thing to do.</p><p>Grand Theft Auto has experimented with these little human exercises for a long time—eating healthy in San Andreas, going on dates in GTA 4—but Rockstar's aims for GTA 6 sound like we'll be making little choices like this constantly. Maybe they'll end up being overboard for some, but I for one can't wait to set out on a mission and realize I need to <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/grand-theft-auto/gta-6-cars-need-gas-ok-im-finally-on-board/">stop for gas</a>.</p><p>There's still no announced PC release date for GTA 6. <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/grand-theft-auto/report-claims-grand-theft-auto-6-will-launch-on-pc-sooner-than-anyone-expected/">Rumor has it</a> that it won't be a long wait, but we'll believe it when we see it. Rockstar usually puts at least seven months between console and PC versions, and it took a year-and-a-half for GTA 5 to come to PC.</p> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/grand-theft-auto/i-feel-like-weve-built-a-pyramid-on-everest-says-rockstar-of-gta-6-meeting-impossible-expectations/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ "We've not compromised on the scale, the detail, the interactivity, the story, the open world." ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">Ssn3rWeRNT4PAygDLv5SFQ</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/mRhauLDDkxHxghWg6ZZms-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:35:52 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                <updated>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 01:11:00 +0000</updated>
                                                                                                                                            <category><![CDATA[Grand Theft Auto]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Games]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Action]]></category>
                                                                                                                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Morgan Park ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/VVB5GCgA3xLhkX8FVAWw5D-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ null ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/mRhauLDDkxHxghWg6ZZms-1920-80.jpg">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[Rockstar Games]]></media:credit>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:description><![CDATA[GTA 6 protagonist Lucia Caminos.]]></media:description>                                                            <media:text><![CDATA[GTA 6 protagonist Lucia Caminos.]]></media:text>
                                <media:title type="plain"><![CDATA[GTA 6 protagonist Lucia Caminos.]]></media:title>
                                                    </media:content>
                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/mRhauLDDkxHxghWg6ZZms-1920-80.jpg" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <p>It is not hyperbole to say that GTA 6 is the most anticipated videogame of all time. That'll happen when one of the most acclaimed game developers of all time takes 13 years to finally put out a new game in one of the most popular series of all time.</p><p>That's a hell of a lot of pressure for the army of developers at Rockstar. In a conversation with our friends at Edge for <a href="https://www.gamesradar.com/edge/gtavi-cover/" target="_blank">the magazine's big inside look at GTA 6</a>, Rockstar North head of development Aaron Garbut spoke about meeting the series' absurd standards.</p><p>"We can't just trot out something that's what people might expect, or that was the easy thing to do," he says. "We've not compromised on the scale, the detail, the interactivity, the story, the open world."</p><p>Despite the studio's famously secretive posture, Garbut says the team is very much aware of the galactic expectations, and deployed an illustrative metaphor to communicate how he thinks they've managed to meet them.</p><p>"I feel like we've built a pyramid on Everest."</p><p>While my mind instantly goes to an eventual GTA 6 mod that'll let me ride a giant pyramid down the biggest mountain in Leonida (will fake Florida have mountains?), I have little reason to doubt Garbut's claims here. Impressions, leaks, and Rockstar's own communications suggest that GTA 6 is doubling down on the systemic details that elevated <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/red-dead-redemption-2-review/">Red Dead Redemption 2</a> from 'GTA with horses' to a crime-forward life sim.</p><p>That game's missions were Rockstar's familiar brand of organized crime, but the things you spent time doing between them were quite new for a mainstream game: Eating, drinking, grooming yourself, camping, browsing, and making small talk with locals. These actions often had some gameplay ramifications, but it was common to perform because it felt like the human thing to do.</p><p>Grand Theft Auto has experimented with these little human exercises for a long time—eating healthy in San Andreas, going on dates in GTA 4—but Rockstar's aims for GTA 6 sound like we'll be making little choices like this constantly. Maybe they'll end up being overboard for some, but I for one can't wait to set out on a mission and realize I need to <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/grand-theft-auto/gta-6-cars-need-gas-ok-im-finally-on-board/">stop for gas</a>.</p><p>There's still no announced PC release date for GTA 6. <a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/grand-theft-auto/report-claims-grand-theft-auto-6-will-launch-on-pc-sooner-than-anyone-expected/">Rumor has it</a> that it won't be a long wait, but we'll believe it when we see it. Rockstar usually puts at least seven months between console and PC versions, and it took a year-and-a-half for GTA 5 to come to PC.</p>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ GTA 6's map is almost as big as Rockstar's last 3 games combined, contains 'an order of magnitude more interiors' ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <p>I knew Grand Theft Auto 6's map was going to be big, but I hadn't expected Rockstar to proclaim that it is, in fact, almost as big as the maps from its last three games combined. An absolute whopper of a <a href="https://www.gamesradar.com/edge/gtavi-cover/">feature in the latest Edge magazine</a> revealed a little bit about the sheer scale of Leonida, and <em>hoo-boy, </em>is it a big one.</p><p>Vice City and its surrounding areas are said to be almost as big as Grand Theft Auto 4, Grand Theft Auto 5, <em>and </em>Red Dead Redemption 2 combined. Which, considering the size of the latter two, is saying something.</p><p>But as we all know, quantity does not necessarily mean quality, and boasts about the size of a videogame world are sometimes followed by empty, unexciting expanses. Rockstar seems keen to express that GTA 6's map is not just sprawling, but also dense.</p><p>Co-studio head Aaron Garbut told Edge that Grand Theft Auto 6 contains "an order of magnitude more interiors" than the developer's previous games, for a start. That's something I'm pretty excited about personally, as someone who delights in interior design and absolutely hates running head-first into fake doors like Wile E. Coyote barrelling into painted tunnels. </p><p>It's not just interiors that have been given a lot of love, though. "Every back alley is as densely detailed and interesting as the others," Garbut says. "You can go anywhere, any random location, and so many people have thought about that location." </p><p>The tepid reception to the scarce stretches of Grand Theft Auto 5's northern areas like Senora Desert informed the creation of Leonida's outer reaches, too, which gives me hope that even Leonida's more barren biomes will have plenty to offer.</p><figure role="gallery"><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/QHZdy4s79XQJcVCoyzEnAf-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 Port Gellhorn screenshot" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/cvwjuWSQa3pRDSHyG2roXo-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 Leonida Keys screenshot" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/9pDAzpntNnfZrmZwFU6oBo-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 Leonida Keys screenshot" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/xLJX9Gw3B3QEauPSEBqCyn-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 Leonida Keys screenshot" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/2eKG4YZAHVGH4LGP5ZFnPa-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 Vice City screenshot" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/5nud2tgcZqKNBnHUJhcUEa-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 Vice City screenshot" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/wEHUEUhGa27AAtJyYhkM8a-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 Vice City screenshot" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/f8Bk8wAfCBecDiDCiMrTvK-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 location Ambrosia" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure></figure><p>Garbut says that even after years of development, there are still areas he's yet to explore. That sense of minute detail within such a vast landmass is the thing that has me most excited to poke around this fictional Florida—from soaking in every tongue-in-cheek parodied brand plastered across billboards, to the pockets of life that'll undoubtedly populate street corners and back alleys. If Leonida is as rich as Garbut describes, then I imagine I'll be spending an awful lot of time making note of every little touch. </p><p>As for when we can do that <em>on PC</em>, there's still no official word—<a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/grand-theft-auto/report-claims-grand-theft-auto-6-will-launch-on-pc-sooner-than-anyone-expected/">only a rumor</a> that the wait won't be long. We're not placing any bets at this point. A seven month gap between console and PC is typical for Rockstar, and GTA 5 took a year-and-a-half to make the jump.</p> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/grand-theft-auto/gta-6s-map-is-almost-as-big-as-rockstars-last-3-games-combined-contains-an-order-of-magnitude-more-interiors/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ "You can go anywhere, any random location, and so many people have thought about that location," says co-studio head Aaron Garbut. ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">U8AU5XD6KA9xjLoqNfFYEm</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/bHe66wF8tgDouaPVeRottY-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:17:15 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                <updated>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:54:09 +0000</updated>
                                                                                                                                            <category><![CDATA[Grand Theft Auto]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Games]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Action]]></category>
                                                                                                                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Mollie Taylor ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/W9VNF2qWSreZXDkwcVR2tF-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
                                                                <dc:description><![CDATA[ null ]]></dc:description>
                                                                                                                                <cf:isSponsored>false</cf:isSponsored>
                <cf:hasAffiliateLinks>false</cf:hasAffiliateLinks>
                <cf:isPaid>false</cf:isPaid>
                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/bHe66wF8tgDouaPVeRottY-1920-80.jpg">
                                                            <media:credit><![CDATA[Rockstar Games]]></media:credit>
                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    <media:description><![CDATA[Grand Theft Auto 6 gameplay reveal]]></media:description>                                                            <media:text><![CDATA[Grand Theft Auto 6 gameplay reveal]]></media:text>
                                <media:title type="plain"><![CDATA[Grand Theft Auto 6 gameplay reveal]]></media:title>
                                                    </media:content>
                                                    <media:thumbnail url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/bHe66wF8tgDouaPVeRottY-1920-80.jpg" />
                                                                                                                                                                    <content:encoded >
                            <![CDATA[
                            <article>
                                <p>I knew Grand Theft Auto 6's map was going to be big, but I hadn't expected Rockstar to proclaim that it is, in fact, almost as big as the maps from its last three games combined. An absolute whopper of a <a href="https://www.gamesradar.com/edge/gtavi-cover/">feature in the latest Edge magazine</a> revealed a little bit about the sheer scale of Leonida, and <em>hoo-boy, </em>is it a big one.</p><p>Vice City and its surrounding areas are said to be almost as big as Grand Theft Auto 4, Grand Theft Auto 5, <em>and </em>Red Dead Redemption 2 combined. Which, considering the size of the latter two, is saying something.</p><p>But as we all know, quantity does not necessarily mean quality, and boasts about the size of a videogame world are sometimes followed by empty, unexciting expanses. Rockstar seems keen to express that GTA 6's map is not just sprawling, but also dense.</p><p>Co-studio head Aaron Garbut told Edge that Grand Theft Auto 6 contains "an order of magnitude more interiors" than the developer's previous games, for a start. That's something I'm pretty excited about personally, as someone who delights in interior design and absolutely hates running head-first into fake doors like Wile E. Coyote barrelling into painted tunnels. </p><p>It's not just interiors that have been given a lot of love, though. "Every back alley is as densely detailed and interesting as the others," Garbut says. "You can go anywhere, any random location, and so many people have thought about that location." </p><p>The tepid reception to the scarce stretches of Grand Theft Auto 5's northern areas like Senora Desert informed the creation of Leonida's outer reaches, too, which gives me hope that even Leonida's more barren biomes will have plenty to offer.</p><figure role="gallery"><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/QHZdy4s79XQJcVCoyzEnAf-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 Port Gellhorn screenshot" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/cvwjuWSQa3pRDSHyG2roXo-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 Leonida Keys screenshot" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/9pDAzpntNnfZrmZwFU6oBo-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 Leonida Keys screenshot" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/xLJX9Gw3B3QEauPSEBqCyn-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 Leonida Keys screenshot" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/2eKG4YZAHVGH4LGP5ZFnPa-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 Vice City screenshot" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/5nud2tgcZqKNBnHUJhcUEa-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 Vice City screenshot" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/wEHUEUhGa27AAtJyYhkM8a-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 Vice City screenshot" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/f8Bk8wAfCBecDiDCiMrTvK-1920-80.jpg" alt="GTA 6 location Ambrosia" /><figcaption><small role="credit">Rockstar Games</small></figcaption></figure></figure><p>Garbut says that even after years of development, there are still areas he's yet to explore. That sense of minute detail within such a vast landmass is the thing that has me most excited to poke around this fictional Florida—from soaking in every tongue-in-cheek parodied brand plastered across billboards, to the pockets of life that'll undoubtedly populate street corners and back alleys. If Leonida is as rich as Garbut describes, then I imagine I'll be spending an awful lot of time making note of every little touch. </p><p>As for when we can do that <em>on PC</em>, there's still no official word—<a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/grand-theft-auto/report-claims-grand-theft-auto-6-will-launch-on-pc-sooner-than-anyone-expected/">only a rumor</a> that the wait won't be long. We're not placing any bets at this point. A seven month gap between console and PC is typical for Rockstar, and GTA 5 took a year-and-a-half to make the jump.</p>
                                                            </article>
                            ]]>
                        </content:encoded>
                                                </item>
                                <item>
                                                            <title><![CDATA[ Can you name the horror games these deeply unpleasant bathrooms are from? ]]></title>
                                                                                                <dc:content><![CDATA[ <p>The second scariest thing about any haunted house is always the bathroom, with the first obviously being closet doors that are ever so slightly ajar. Public restrooms are scary in general, but homes always have some manner of bathroom cryptid playing peekaboo with the shower curtain, and I can't handle that. </p><div  class="fancy-box"><div class="fancy_box-title">More quizzes!</div><div class="fancy_box_body"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' ><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:56.25%;"><img id="XHdkj6AKzQwnn4rGxre4K4" name="logo_quiz" caption="" alt="The PC Gamer Quiz logo in green" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/XHdkj6AKzQwnn4rGxre4K4-1920-80.png" mos="" link="" align="" fullscreen="" width="" height="" attribution="" endorsement="" class="pinterest-pin-exclude" /></p></div></div><figcaption itemprop="caption description" class=""><span class="credit" itemprop="copyrightHolder">(Image credit: Future)</span></figcaption></figure><p class="fancy-box__body-text">Want to keep testing your knowledge of gaming trivia? We've got loads more <a data-analytics-id="inline-link" href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/think-you-know-gaming-test-your-knowledge-with-pc-gamers-fiendish-quizzes/" target="_blank">PC Gamer quizzes</a>, on everything from healthbars to weird currencies to absurd patch notes.</p></div></div><p>It's also where a lot of horror games love to send us, whether it's for a good ol' fashioned jumpscare from apparitions in a mirror or just a particularly unsanitary commode. There's also the underrated sink baby gag from P.T., so you can't even wash your hands without developing a complex. </p><p><strong>You've got 12 minutes to identify the 14 horror games these gross restrooms are from. </strong>When you're done, let us know how you did! If you get a perfect score, I promise to start calling you 'bathroom boss,' but anything less than that and I'm flushing you down the toilet. </p><div style="min-height: 640px;">                                <div class="kwizly-quiz kwizly-XbPggW"></div>                            </div>                            <script src="https://kwizly.com/embed/XbPggW.js" async=""></script><div class="product"><a data-dimension112="eab82a54-d321-11f1-978e-d7376697dd5d" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="2026 games" data-dimension48="2026 games" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><figure class="van-image-figure "  ><div class='image-full-width-wrapper'><div class='image-widthsetter' style="max-width:661px;"><p class="vanilla-image-block" style="padding-top:98.94%;"><img id="6offQUY4CXebir2TC27dMd" name="kingdom come 2 square" caption="" alt="" src="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/6offQUY4CXebir2TC27dMd-1920-80.jpg" mos="" align="middle" fullscreen="" width="661" height="654" attribution="" endorsement="" credit="" class="" /></p></div></div></figure></a><p><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/games/new-pc-games-2026/" target="_blank" data-dimension112="eab82a54-d321-11f1-978e-d7376697dd5d" data-action="Deal Block" data-label="2026 games" data-dimension48="2026 games" data-dimension25=""><strong>2026 games</strong></a>: All the upcoming games<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/the-best-pc-games/" target="_blank"><strong>Best PC games</strong></a>: Our all-time favorites<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/the-50-best-free-pc-games/" target="_blank"><strong>Free PC games</strong></a>: Freebie fest<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/best-fps-games/" target="_blank"><strong>Best FPS games</strong></a>: Finest gunplay<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/best-rpgs-of-all-time/" target="_blank"><strong>Best RPGs</strong></a>: Grand adventures<br /><a href="https://www.pcgamer.com/the-best-co-op-games/" target="_blank"><strong>Best co-op games</strong></a>: Better together</p></div> ]]></dc:content>
                                                                                                                                            <link>https://www.pcgamer.com/games/horror/can-you-name-the-horror-game-these-deeply-unpleasant-bathrooms-are-from/</link>
                                                                            <description>
                            <![CDATA[ Bring holy water and Clorox wipes ]]>
                                                                                                            </description>
                                                                                                                                <guid isPermaLink="false">soZRKZmxVo9MBV4ds2RVmj</guid>
                                                                                                <enclosure url="https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/jGgQPA6L6k3Cc6i2nqLZQD-1920-80.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"></enclosure>
                                                                        <pubDate>Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:50:34 +0000</pubDate>                                                                                                                                <updated>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:10:31 +0000</updated>
                                                                                                                                            <category><![CDATA[Horror]]></category>
                                                    <category><![CDATA[Games]]></category>
                                                                                                                    <dc:creator><![CDATA[ Andrea Shearon ]]></dc:creator>                                                                                    <dc:source><![CDATA[ https://cdn.mos.cms.futurecdn.net/qGDcAqeJDHFab8LYduM29E-320-70.png ]]></dc:source>
